window.READING_DATA = [{"id":"eng1_2021_t4","exam":"英语一","year":"2021","text_num":"Text 4","title":"宽带网络服务商垄断与网络中立性","difficulty":"困难★★★★★","summary":"探讨美国联邦通信委员会（FCC）2017年废除网络中立性规则后引发的司法与州级法律博弈，分析宽带商潜在的反竞争行为，并呼吁国会立法明确监管授权。","paragraphs":["From the early days of broadband, advocates for consumers and web-based companies worried that the cable and phone companies selling broadband connections had the power and incentive to favor affiliated websites over their rivals'. That's why there has been such a strong demand for rules that would prevent broadband providers from picking winners and losers online, preserving the freedom and innovation that have been the lifeblood of the Internet.","Yet that demand has been almost impossible to fill-in part because of pushback from broadband providers, anti-regulatory conservatives and the courts. A federal appeals court weighed in again Tuesday, but instead of providing a badly needed resolution, it only prolonged the fight. At issue before the U.S. Court of Appeals for the District of Columbia Circuit was the latest take of the Federal Communications Commission (FCC) on net neutrality, adopted on a party-line vote in 2017. The Republican-penned order not only eliminated the strict net neutrality rules the FCC had adopted when it had a Democratic majority in 2015, but rejected the commission's authority to require broadband providers to do much of anything. The order also declared that state and local governments couldn't regulate broadband providers either.","The commission argued that other agencies would protect against anti-competitive behavior, such as a broadband-providing conglomerate like AT&T favoring its own video-streaming service at the expense of Netflix and Apple TV. Yet the FCC also ended the investigations of broadband providers that imposed data caps on their rivals' streaming services but not their own.","On Tuesday, the appeals court unanimously upheld the 2017 order deregulating broadband providers, citing a Supreme Court ruling from 2005 that upheld a similarly deregulatory move. But Judge Patricia Millett rightly argued in a concurring opinion that \"the result is unhinged from the realities of modern broadband service,\" and said Congress or the Supreme Court could intervene to \"avoid trapping Internet regulation in technological anachronism.\"","In the meantime, the court threw out the FCC's attempt to block all state rules on net neutrality, while preserving the commission's power to preempt individual state laws that undermine its order. That means more battles like the one now going on between the Justice Department and California, which enacted a tough net neutrality law in the wake of the FCC's abdication.","The endless legal battles and back-and-forth at the FCC cry out for Congress to act. It needs to give the commission explicit authority once and for all to bar broadband providers from meddling in the traffic on their network and to create clear rules protecting openness and innovation online."],"questions":[{"q_num":36,"stem":"There has long been concern that broadband providers would","options":{"A":"bring web-based firms under control.","B":"slow down the traffic on their network.","C":"show partiality in treating clients.","D":"intensify competition with their rivals."},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":1,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第1段首句：消费者和网络公司倡导者一直担心，宽带提供商有能力和动机偏袒关联网站、冷落对手（favor affiliated websites over their rivals'），即对待客户有失偏颇（show partiality in treating clients）。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偷换概念】第1段说宽带商有动机偏袒关联网站（favor affiliated websites），并非要把网络公司置于自己控制之下（bring web-based firms under control）。","B":"【无中生有】第1段并未提及宽带商故意降低网络流量速度（slow down the traffic）。","C":"【正解】第1段首句指出宽带商有能力和动机偏袒关联网站、打压竞争对手，第二句将其概括为“picking winners and losers online”，精准对应 show partiality in treating clients（在对待客户时表现出偏袒）。","D":"【正反混淆】原文担忧的是宽带商偏袒自家关联网站、破坏公平竞争，而不是加剧与竞争对手的竞争（intensify competition with their rivals）。"}},{"q_num":37,"stem":"Faced with the demand for net neutrality rules, the FCC","options":{"A":"sticks to an out-of-date order.","B":"takes an anti-regulatory stance.","C":"has issued a special resolution.","D":"has allowed the states to intervene."},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":2,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第2段后两句：共和党起草的2017年命令不仅废除了2015年严格的网络中立性规则，还否认了FCC要求宽带商履行监管义务的权限，体现其反监管立场（anti-regulatory stance）。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偷换概念】第2段指出FCC在2017年主动推翻了2015年的旧规则并解除管制，并非“固守过时命令（sticks to an out-of-date order）”。","B":"【正解】第2段明确说明FCC的2017年命令废除了严格的网络中立性规则（eliminated the strict net neutrality rules）、放弃了自身监管权（rejected the commission's authority），并阻止州和地方政府监管，充分体现其反监管立场（takes an anti-regulatory stance）。","C":"【正反混淆】第2段第二句明确指出联邦上诉法院未能提供亟需的解决方案（instead of providing a badly needed resolution），且FCC并未发布所谓“特别决议（special resolution）”。","D":"【正反混淆】第2段末句称该命令宣称州和地方政府也不得监管宽带商（couldn't regulate broadband providers either），是禁止而非允许各州干预。"}},{"q_num":38,"stem":"What can be learned about AT&T from Paragraph 3?","options":{"A":"It protects against unfair competition.","B":"It engages in anti-competitive practices.","C":"It is under the FCC's investigation.","D":"It is in pursuit of quality service."},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":3,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第3段首句：原文将AT&T作为反竞争行为（anti-competitive behavior）的典型例子，指出其偏袒自家视频流媒体服务、排挤Netflix和Apple TV。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【张冠李戴】第3段说的是FCC声称“其他机构（other agencies）”会防范反竞争行为，而AT&T本身是被举作反竞争行为的例子，并非保护公平竞争的主体。","B":"【正解】第3段首句明确举例称，像AT&T这样的宽带巨头偏袒自家视频流媒体服务、损害Netflix和Apple TV的利益，属于反竞争行为（anti-competitive behavior），对应 engages in anti-competitive practices。","C":"【正反混淆】第3段末句指出FCC已经“终止了调查（ended the investigations）”，而非AT&T目前正在接受FCC调查。","D":"【无中生有】第3段围绕反竞争与数据流量上限展开，并未提及AT&T追求优质服务（in pursuit of quality service）。"}},{"q_num":39,"stem":"Judge Patricia Millett argues that the appeals court's decision","options":{"A":"focuses on trivialities.","B":"conveys an ambiguous message.","C":"is at odds with its earlier rulings.","D":"is out of touch with reality."},"answer":"D","hint":{"para":4,"type":"观点态度题","focus":"定位第4段第二句：法官Patricia Millett在赞同意见书中指出，这一裁决结果脱离现代宽带服务的现实（unhinged from the realities of modern broadband service），对应 is out of touch with reality。"},"question_type":"观点态度题","option_analysis":{"A":"【无中生有】法官并未批评判决纠结于细枝末节（focuses on trivialities），而是批评其脱离现代宽带技术现实。","B":"【无中生有】原文未提及判决传递了含糊不清的信息（ambiguous message）；上诉法院是一致维持（unanimously upheld）了2017年命令。","C":"【正反混淆】第4段首句明确提到上诉法院援引了2005年最高法院的类似判例（citing a Supreme Court ruling from 2005 that upheld a similarly deregulatory move），并非与先前判例矛盾，而是与现实脱节。","D":"【正解】第4段法官Patricia Millett直言裁决结果“is unhinged from the realities of modern broadband service”，并警示避免让互联网监管陷入时代错位（technological anachronism），精准对应 is out of touch with reality（脱离现实）。"}},{"q_num":40,"stem":"What does the author argue in the last paragraph?","options":{"A":"Congress needs to take action to ensure net neutrality.","B":"The FCC should be put under strict supervision.","C":"Rules need to be set to diversify online services.","D":"Broadband providers' rights should be protected."},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":6,"type":"观点态度题","focus":"定位第6段：面对无休止的法律拉锯，作者呼吁国会采取行动（cry out for Congress to act），赋予FCC明确权限、制定清晰规则保护网络开放与创新。"},"question_type":"观点态度题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第6段明确提出“cry out for Congress to act”，要求国会一次性赋予FCC明确权限，禁止宽带商干预网络流量并建立清晰规则保护网络开放与创新，即国会需要采取行动以保障网络中立性（Congress needs to take action to ensure net neutrality）。","B":"【偷换概念】末段主张国会赋予FCC明确监管权（give the commission explicit authority），而非把FCC置于严格监督之下（put under strict supervision）。","C":"【偷换概念】制定清晰规则的目的是保护网络开放与创新（protecting openness and innovation online），而非为了使在线服务多样化（diversify online services）。","D":"【正反混淆】全文及末段均主张限制宽带商干预网络流量（bar broadband providers from meddling in the traffic），而非保护宽带商的权利。"}}],"detailed_analysis":"本文围绕美国网络中立性（Net Neutrality）之争展开。FCC在2017年推翻了2015年严格的网络中立性规则并放弃监管权，还试图禁止各州自行监管。联邦上诉法院虽维持了FCC解除管制的命令，但法官Patricia Millett指出该裁决脱离现代宽带现实，同时法院驳回了FCC全面封杀州法的企图。作者最终呼吁国会正式立法，赋予FCC明确权限以维护网络开放与创新。","keywords":[{"word":"broadband","trans":"n. 宽带网络"},{"word":"net neutrality","trans":"n. 网络中立性"},{"word":"affiliated","trans":"adj. 附属的，有关联的"},{"word":"deregulatory","trans":"adj. 解除管制的"},{"word":"anachronism","trans":"n. 时代错误，过时的人或事"},{"word":"abdication","trans":"n. 放弃职责，退位"}]},{"id":"eng1_2022_t4","exam":"英语一","year":"2022","text_num":"Text 4","title":"新西兰《雇佣关系法》与高薪员工解雇争议","difficulty":"困难★★★★★","summary":"剖析新西兰《雇佣关系法》（ERA）中的个人申诉条款在适用于高薪高管时引发的悖论：限制企业解雇失职高管反而损害生产力、工人工资、招聘意愿及社会整体福祉。","paragraphs":["The personal grievance provisions of New Zealand's Employment Relations Act 2000 (ERA) prevent an employer from firing an employee without good cause. Instead, dismissals must be justified. Employers must both show cause and act in a procedurally fair way.","Personal grievance procedures were designed to guard the jobs of ordinary workers from \"unjustified dismissals\". The premise was that the common law of contract lacked sufficient safeguards for workers against arbitrary conduct by management. Long gone are the days when a boss could simply give an employee contractual notice.","But these provisions create difficulties for businesses when applied to highly paid managers and executives. As countless boards and business owners will attest, constraining firms from firing poorly performing, high-earning managers is a handbrake on boosting productivity and overall performance. The difference between C-grade and A-grade managers may very well be the difference between business success or failure. Between preserving the jobs of ordinary workers or losing them. Yet mediocrity is no longer enough to justify a dismissal.","Consequently- and paradoxically- laws introduced to protect the jobs of ordinary workers may be placing those jobs at risk.","If not placing jobs at risk, to the extent employment protection laws constrain business owners from dismissing underperforming managers, those laws act as a constraint on firm productivity and therefore on workers' wages. Indeed, in “An International Perspective on New Zealand's Productivity Paradox” (2014), the Productivity Commission singled out the low quality of managerial capabilities as a cause of the country's poor productivity growth record.","Nor are highly paid managers themselves immune from the harm caused by the ERA's unjustified dismissal procedures. Because employment protection laws make it costlier to fire an employee, employers are more cautious about hiring new staff. This makes it harder for the marginal manager to gain employment. And firms pay staff less because firms carry the burden of the employment arrangement going wrong.","Society also suffers from excessive employment protections. Stringent job dismissal regulations adversely affect productivity growth and hamper both prosperity and overall well-being.","Across the Tasman Sea, Australia deals with the unjustified dismissal paradox by excluding employees earning above a specified \"high-income threshold\" from the protection of its unfair dismissal laws. In New Zealand, a 2016 private members' Bill tried to permit firms and high-income employees to contract out of the unjustified dismissal regime. However, the mechanisms proposed were unwieldy and the Bill was voted down following the change in government later that year."],"questions":[{"q_num":36,"stem":"The personal grievance provisions of the ERA are intended to","options":{"A":"punish dubious corporate practices.","B":"improve traditional hiring procedures.","C":"exempt employers from certain duties.","D":"protect the rights of ordinary workers."},"answer":"D","hint":{"para":2,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第1–2段：ERA个人申诉条款要求解雇必须有正当理由且程序公正，第2段首句明确指出其设计初衷是保护普通工人免遭不当解雇（guard the jobs of ordinary workers from \"unjustified dismissals\"）。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【无中生有】第1–2段并未提及惩罚可疑企业行为（punish dubious corporate practices），而是聚焦防止无正当理由解雇。","B":"【偷换概念】条款规范的是解雇（dismissals）的正当理由与程序公正，而非改进传统招聘流程（hiring procedures）。","C":"【正反混淆】第1段要求雇主证明解雇有理且程序公正，是增加而非豁免雇主义务（exempt employers from certain duties）。","D":"【正解】第2段首句明确指出个人申诉程序旨在保护普通工人工作免遭不当解雇（guard the jobs of ordinary workers from \"unjustified dismissals\"），防范管理层武断行为，对应 protect the rights of ordinary workers。"}},{"q_num":37,"stem":"It can be learned from Paragraph 3 that the provisions may","options":{"A":"hinder business development.","B":"undermine managers' authority.","C":"affect the public image of the firms.","D":"worsen labor-management relations."},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":3,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第3段前两句：将这些条款适用于高薪高管会给企业带来困难（create difficulties for businesses），限制企业解雇不称职高管成为提升生产力和整体业绩的“手刹/阻碍”（a handbrake on boosting productivity and overall performance）。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第3段指出，限制企业解雇表现不佳的高薪管理者，无异于给提升生产力和整体表现拉上手刹（a handbrake on boosting productivity and overall performance），甚至关乎企业成败，对应 hinder business development（阻碍企业发展）。","B":"【无中生有】第3段讨论的是难以解雇平庸高管对企业经营的拖累，并未提及削弱管理者的权威（undermine managers' authority）。","C":"【无中生有】第3段完全没有涉及企业的公众形象（public image）。","D":"【无中生有】第3段未提及劳资关系恶化（worsen labor-management relations）。"}},{"q_num":38,"stem":"Which of the following measures would the Productivity Commission support?","options":{"A":"Imposing reasonable wage restraints.","B":"Enforcing employment protection laws.","C":"Limiting the powers of business owners.","D":"Dismissing poorly performing managers."},"answer":"D","hint":{"para":5,"type":"推断题","focus":"定位第5段：上句指出限制企业主解雇表现不佳的管理者会制约生产力和工资，紧接着用“Indeed”引出生产力委员会的报告，点出管理能力低下（low quality of managerial capabilities）是生产力增长乏力的原因，由此推断该委员会支持解雇不称职高管。"},"question_type":"推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正反混淆】第5段认为就业保护法压低了工人工资是负面后果，生产力委员会关注的是提升管理质量与生产力，并未主张实施工资限制（wage restraints）。","B":"【正反混淆】第5段将就业保护法视为制约企业生产力的束缚（constraint on firm productivity），委员会不会支持继续强化此类限制性条款。","C":"【正反混淆】原文批评就业保护法过度束缚企业主解雇失职高管的权力，而非主张进一步限制企业主权力。","D":"【正解】第5段指出生产力委员会在报告中特别指明低质量的管理能力拖累了国家生产力增长，呼应本段首句“限制企业主解雇表现不佳的管理者会制约生产力”，可推知该委员会支持解雇表现不佳的管理者（Dismissing poorly performing managers）。"}},{"q_num":39,"stem":"What might be an effect of ERA's unjustified dismissal procedures?","options":{"A":"Highly paid managers lose their jobs.","B":"Employees suffer from salary cuts.","C":"Society sees a rise in overall well-being.","D":"Employers need to hire new staff."},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":6,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第6段末句：由于企业需要承担雇佣关系出错的风险和成本，企业会向员工支付更低的工资（And firms pay staff less because firms carry the burden of the employment arrangement going wrong）。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正反混淆】第6段说解雇成本高使雇主对招聘更谨慎，导致边缘管理者更难获得工作（harder for the marginal manager to gain employment），并非现有高薪管理者失去工作。","B":"【正解】第6段末句明确指出，由于企业独自承担用工出错的成本，企业会给员工支付更低的薪酬（firms pay staff less），且第5段亦提到相关法律制约了工人工资，精准对应 Employees suffer from salary cuts。","C":"【正反混淆】第7段指出严苛的解雇规定会妨碍繁荣和整体福祉（hamper both prosperity and overall well-being），是下降而非上升。","D":"【正反混淆】第6段指出雇主对招聘新人更加谨慎（more cautious about hiring new staff），并非需要招聘新员工。"}},{"q_num":40,"stem":"It can be inferred that the \"high-income threshold\" in Australia","options":{"A":"has secured managers' earnings.","B":"has produced undesired results.","C":"is beneficial to business owners.","D":"is difficult to put into practice."},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":8,"type":"推断题","focus":"定位第8段首句：澳大利亚通过设定“高收入门槛”，将高于该门槛的员工排除在不公平解雇法保护之外，从而破解“不当解雇悖论”，解除企业主解雇失职高管的束缚，对企业主有利（is beneficial to business owners）。"},"question_type":"推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偷换概念】澳大利亚的高收入门槛是把高收入员工排除在不公平解雇法保护之外，并非保障管理者的收入（secured managers' earnings）。","B":"【无中生有】第8段将澳大利亚的做法作为解决不当解雇悖论的对策来介绍，并未提及该机制产生了不良后果（undesired results）。","C":"【正解】前文反复论述不当解雇条款束缚了企业主解雇失职高管、拖累经营；第8段首句指出澳大利亚将超过高收入门槛的员工排除在不公平解雇法保护之外，赋予企业主更大用人自主权，可推断该门槛对企业主有利（is beneficial to business owners）。","D":"【张冠李戴】第8段后两句提到的“机制笨拙（unwieldy）”并被否决的，是新西兰2016年的议员私人法案（2016 private members' Bill），而非澳大利亚的高收入门槛。"},"disputed":true,"answerPrimary":"C","answerAlt":"D","disputeNote":"主流解析（新东方等）主推 C（is beneficial to business owners）；另有部分机构/解析主推 D（is difficult to put into practice）。争议焦点在于第 8 段“unwieldy”仅指新西兰私人法案，还是也暗含高收入门槛难以落地。"}],"detailed_analysis":"本文探讨新西兰《雇佣关系法》（ERA）个人申诉条款的初衷与现实困境。该条款原意是保护普通工人免遭无正当理由解雇，但套用到高薪管理者身上时，却成为企业提升生产力和经营表现的掣肘，不仅危及普通工人岗位与薪酬，也让边缘管理者更难受雇、拖累社会繁荣。文末对比了澳大利亚的“高收入门槛”机制与新西兰2016年流产的修法提案。","keywords":[{"word":"grievance","trans":"n. 不平，抱怨，申诉"},{"word":"provision","trans":"n. 条款，规定"},{"word":"payout","trans":"n. 支出，巨额赔偿金"},{"word":"salaried","trans":"adj. 有薪金的"},{"word":"vulnerable","trans":"adj. 脆弱的，易受伤害的"},{"word":"remedy","trans":"n./v. 补救，救济"}]},{"id":"eng1_2023_t3","exam":"英语一","year":"2023","text_num":"Text 3","title":"水石书店与出版商的渠道博弈战","difficulty":"困难★★★★★","summary":"剖析英国最大连锁书店水石书店（Waterstones）与出版巨头企鹅兰登书屋（PRH）因信贷额度限制引发的商业僵局，以及该争端和大型出版商并购潮对中游作者与出版生态多元化的威胁。","paragraphs":["If you're heading for your nearest branch of Waterstones, the biggest book retailer in the UK, in search of the Duchess of Sussex's new children's book The Bench, you might have to be prepared to hunt around a bit; the same may be true of The President's Daughter, the new thriller by Bill Clinton and James Patterson. Both of these books are published next week by Penguin Random House (PRH), a company currently involved in a stand-off with Waterstones.","The problem began late last year, when PRH confirmed that it had introduced a credit limit with Waterstones \"at a very significant level.\" The trade magazine The Bookseller reported that Waterstones branch managers were being told to remove PRH books from prominent areas such as tables, display spaces and windows, and were \"quietly retiring them to their relevant sections\".","PRH declined to comment on the issue, but a spokesperson for Waterstones told me: \"Waterstones are currently operating with reduced credit terms from PRH, the only publisher in the UK to place any limitations on our ability to trade. We are not boycotting PRH titles but we are doing our utmost to ensure that availability for customers remains good despite the lower overall levels of stock. We are hopeful with our shops now open again that normality will return and that we will be allowed to buy appropriately. Certainly, our shops are exceptionally busy. The sales for our May Books of the Month surpassed any month since 2018.”","In the meantime, PRH authors have been the losers. Big-name PRH authors may suffer a bit, but it's those mid-list authors, who normally rely on Waterstones staff's passion for promoting books by lesser-known writers, who will be praying for an end to the dispute.","It comes at a time when authors are already worried about the consequences of the proposed merger between PRH and another big publisher, Simon & Schuster- the reduction in the number of unaligned UK publishers is likely to lead to fewer bidding wars, lower advances, and more conformity in terms of what is published.","\"This is all part of a wider change towards concentration of power,\" says literary agent Andrew Lownie. \"The publishing industry talks about diversity in terms of authors and staff but it also needs a plurality of ways of delivering intellectual contact, choice and different voices. After all, many of the most interesting books in recent years have come from small publishers.\"","We shall see whether that plurality is a casualty of the current need among publishers to be big enough to take on all-comers."],"questions":[{"q_num":31,"stem":"The author mentions two books in Paragraph 1 to present","options":{"A":"an ongoing conflict.","B":"an intellectual concept.","C":"a prevailing sentiment.","D":"a literary phenomenon."},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":1,"type":"例证题","focus":"定位第1段末句：作者先列举在水石书店可能要费劲寻找的两本新书，紧接着点明两本书均由PRH出版，而PRH目前正与水石书店陷入僵持对抗（currently involved in a stand-off with Waterstones）。"},"question_type":"例证题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第1段以读者在水石书店难以直接找到两本新书为引子，末句直接点出出版商PRH正与水石书店陷入僵局（currently involved in a stand-off），“stand-off”精准对应 an ongoing conflict（一场持续的冲突）。","B":"【无中生有】第1段仅呈现具体购书现象与商业对抗，并未借此引出任何知识或思想概念（intellectual concept）。","C":"【无中生有】首段所述为书店与出版商之间的实际商业僵局，并非某种普遍情绪（prevailing sentiment）。","D":"【范围过宽】提及两本新书是为了具体引出PRH与水石书店之间的商业对峙，而非泛泛介绍某种文学现象（literary phenomenon）。"}},{"q_num":32,"stem":"Why did Waterstones shops retire PRH books to their relevant sections?","options":{"A":"To make them easily noticeable.","B":"To comply with PRH's requirement.","C":"To respond to PRH's business move.","D":"To arrange them in a systematic way."},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":2,"type":"因果细节题","focus":"定位第2段：事情始于PRH确认对水石书店施加了极大幅度的信贷限制（introduced a credit limit），随后水石书店经理接到通知将PRH的书撤出显眼展台、悄悄归入常规书架，即回应PRH的商业举措。"},"question_type":"因果细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正反混淆】第2段指出书店将PRH的书从桌子、展区、橱窗等显眼位置撤走（remove PRH books from prominent areas）并悄悄归位，目的恰恰是降低其曝光度，而非使其容易被注意到。","B":"【张冠李戴】下达撤架通知的是水石书店自身管理层，这是针对PRH施加信贷限制的反制措施，而非遵从PRH的要求（comply with PRH's requirement）。","C":"【正解】第2段因果清晰：PRH先对水石书店设置了严苛的信贷额度（business move），水石书店随即通知各分店经理撤下PRH图书的显眼陈列、将其归入普通分区，精准对应 To respond to PRH's business move。","D":"【偷换概念】将书退回对应分类区并非出于常规的“系统化整理陈列（arrange them in a systematic way）”，而是面对PRH限制交易作出的商业应对。"}},{"q_num":33,"stem":"What message does the spokesperson for Waterstones seem to convey?","options":{"A":"Their customers remain loyal.","B":"The credit limit will be removed.","C":"Their stock is underestimated.","D":"The book market is rather slack."},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":3,"type":"推断题","focus":"定位第3段后两句：水石书店发言人强调门店“异常繁忙（exceptionally busy）”，5月“月度精选图书”销量创下2018年以来单月新高，意在传达顾客依然高度忠诚、光顾踊跃。"},"question_type":"推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第3段末尾水石书店发言人特意强调：“Certainly, our shops are exceptionally busy. The sales for our May Books of the Month surpassed any month since 2018.”门店极其繁忙、销量破纪录，清晰传达了其顾客依然忠诚支持（Their customers remain loyal）。","B":"【过度推断】发言人只表示“希望（We are hopeful）”恢复正常并获准合理进货，这仅是主观期盼，并未断言信贷额度一定会被取消（will be removed）。","C":"【偷换概念】发言人承认整体库存水平较低（lower overall levels of stock）但仍尽力保证顾客能买到书，并非声称库存被低估（underestimated）。","D":"【正反混淆】发言人明言门店异常繁忙且5月销量创2018年以来新高，与“图书市场低迷（rather slack）”完全相反。"},"disputed":true,"answerPrimary":"A","answerAlt":"B","disputeNote":"新东方逐篇解析、知乎多数解析主推 A（Their customers remain loyal）；另有部分机构主推 B（The credit limit will be removed，外部部分卷面/资料中该选项记作 C）。"},{"q_num":34,"stem":"What can be one consequence of the current dispute?","options":{"A":"Sales of books by mid-list PRH writers fall off considerably.","B":"Lesser-known PRH writers become the target of criticism.","C":"Waterstones staff hesitate to promote big-name authors' books.","D":"Waterstones branches suffer a severe reduction in revenue."},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":4,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第4段：PRH的作者是这场争端的输家，大牌作者或许只受轻微影响，但平时依赖水石书店员工热情推介的PRH中游作者（mid-list authors）受损最重、迫切祈祷争端结束。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第4段指出PRH作者成为输家（have been the losers），尤其平时依赖水石书店员工推介知名度较低作品的中游作者（mid-list authors）最盼望争端结束，可推知其图书销量大幅下滑，对应 Sales of books by mid-list PRH writers fall off considerably。","B":"【偷换概念】中游/知名度较低的PRH作者是争端的受害者，而非“成为批评的对象（target of criticism）”。","C":"【张冠李戴】第4段说书店员工通常热心推介的是不太知名作者的书（books by lesser-known writers），而非犹豫是否推介大牌作者的书。","D":"【正反混淆】第3段反而指出水石书店门店异常繁忙、销量创2018年以来新高，文中并未提到水石分店营收严重下滑。"}},{"q_num":35,"stem":"Which of the following statements best represents Lownie's view?","options":{"A":"Small publishers ought to stick together.","B":"Big publishers will lose their dominance.","C":"The publishing industry is having a hard time.","D":"The merger of publishers is a worrying trend."},"answer":"D","hint":{"para":6,"type":"观点态度题","focus":"定位第5–6段：第5段提及PRH拟收购西蒙与舒斯特令作者担忧，第6段文学经纪人Andrew Lownie评论“这一切都是权力走向集中的更大趋势的一部分”，并强调出版业需要多元声音，可见他认为出版商合并是令人担忧的趋势。"},"question_type":"观点态度题","option_analysis":{"A":"【无中生有】Lownie肯定了许多有趣书籍出自小出版商，强调行业需要多元声音，但并未主张小出版商应当联合抱团（stick together）。","B":"【正反混淆】第5–6段担忧的是大型出版商合并导致权力进一步集中（concentration of power），而非大出版商将失去主导地位。","C":"【范围过宽】Lownie的批评聚焦于合并带来的权力集中与出版多样性受损，并未笼统宣称整个出版业正在经历困难时期（having a hard time）。","D":"【正解】第5段指出PRH与西蒙与舒斯特拟议合并令作者忧心，第6段Lownie直指“This is all part of a wider change towards concentration of power”，并强调行业离不开多元渠道与不同声音，说明他视出版商合并为令人担忧的趋势（The merger of publishers is a worrying trend）。"}}],"detailed_analysis":"本文以读者在水石书店难以寻觅企鹅兰登书屋（PRH）两本新书切入，揭示PRH大幅收紧对水石书店的信贷额度、水石书店随即撤下PRH图书显眼陈列的商业对抗。尽管水石书店强调销量强劲、顾客支持，但争端已重创依赖店员推荐的PRH中游作者。文末借文学经纪人Andrew Lownie之口指出，PRH拟收购西蒙与舒斯特等大型并购正加剧出版界权力集中，威胁声音与选题的多元化。","keywords":[{"word":"retailer","trans":"n. 零售商"},{"word":"discount","trans":"n./v. 折扣"},{"word":"margin","trans":"n. 利润空间，边缘"},{"word":"independents","trans":"n. 独立实体（书店）"},{"word":"wholesaler","trans":"n. 批发商"},{"word":"distributor","trans":"n. 发行商，分销商"}]},{"id":"eng1_2023_t4","exam":"英语一","year":"2023","text_num":"Text 4","title":"科学论文引用乱象与学术评价机制","difficulty":"困难★★★★★","summary":"揭露学术界唯引用量评价机制催生的“引用卡特尔”、投稿支持咨询机构诱导加引以及“奶牛期刊”等灰色操纵乱象，指出Scopus数据库具备识别能力并呼吁作者坚决拒绝与举报。","paragraphs":["Scientific papers are the recordkeepers of progress in research. Each year researchers publish millions of papers in more than 30,000 journals. The scientific community measures the quality of those papers in a number of ways, including the perceived quality of the journal (as reflected by the title's impact factor) and the number of citations a specific paper accumulates. The careers of scientists and the reputation of their institutions depend on the number and prestige of the papers they produce, but even more so on the citations attracted by these papers.","Citation cartels, where journals, authors, and institutions conspire to inflate citation numbers, have existed for a long time. In 2016, researchers developed an algorithm to recognize suspicious citation patterns, including groups of authors that disproportionately cite one another and groups of journals that cite each other frequently to increase the impact factors of their publications. Recently, another expression of this predatory behavior has emerged: so-called support service consultancies that provide language and other editorial support to individual authors and to journals sometimes advise contributors to add a number of citations to their articles.","The advent of electronic publishing and authors' need to find outlets for their papers resulted in thousands of new journals. The birth of predatory journals wasn't far behind. These journals can act as milk cows where every single article in an issue may cite a specific paper or a series of papers. In some instances, there is absolutely no relationship between the content of the article and the citations. The peculiar part is that the journal that the editor is supposedly working for is not profiting at all—it is just providing citations to other journals. Such practices can lead an article to accrue more than 150 citations in the same year that it was published.","How insidious is this type of citation manipulation? In one example, an individual—acting as author, editor, and consultant—was able to use at least 15 journals as citation providers to articles published by five scientists at three universities. The problem is rampant in Scopus, a citation database, which includes a high number of the new \"international\" journals. In fact, a listing in Scopus seems to be a criterion to be targeted in this type of citation manipulation.","Scopus itself has all the data necessary to detect this malpractice. Red flags include a large number of citations to an article within the first year. And for authors who wish to steer clear of citation cartel activities: when an editor, a reviewer, or a support service asks you to add inappropriate references, do not oblige and do report the request to the journal."],"questions":[{"q_num":36,"stem":"According to Paragraph 1, the careers of scientists can be determined by","options":{"A":"how many citations their works contain.","B":"how many times their papers are cited.","C":"the prestige of the people they work with.","D":"the status they have in scientific circles."},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":1,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第1段末句：科学家的职业生涯与所属机构声誉取决于其发表论文的数量和声望，但更重要的是取决于这些论文所获得的引用次数（even more so on the citations attracted by these papers）。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偷换概念】原文指论文所“获得/吸引”的被引次数（citations attracted by these papers），而A项说论文自身“包含”多少引用（citations their works contain），主被动关系完全颠倒。","B":"【正解】第1段末句明确指出，科学家的职业生涯更取决于论文吸引的引用次数（the citations attracted by these papers），精准对应 how many times their papers are cited。","C":"【偷换概念】原文“prestige of the papers they produce”指所发论文的声望，而非合作同事的声望（prestige of the people they work with）。","D":"【张冠李戴】第1段末句说“the reputation of their institutions depend on...”意为机构声誉取决于论文和引用，而非科学家在学界的地位决定其职业生涯，因果与对象皆错。"}},{"q_num":37,"stem":"The support service consultancies tend to","options":{"A":"recommend journals to their clients.","B":"list citation patterns for their clients.","C":"ask authors to include extra citations.","D":"advise contributors to cite each other."},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":2,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第2段末句：所谓的支持服务咨询机构（support service consultancies）有时会建议投稿人在文章中额外增加若干引用（advise contributors to add a number of citations to their articles）。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【无中生有】第2段指出这些咨询机构提供语言和编辑支持并建议加引，并未提及向客户推荐期刊（recommend journals）。","B":"【张冠李戴】识别可疑引用模式（citation patterns）是2016年研究者开发的算法的功能，而非咨询机构为客户列举引用模式。","C":"【正解】第2段末句明确提到“so-called support service consultancies... sometimes advise contributors to add a number of citations to their articles”，直接同义替换为 ask authors to include extra citations。","D":"【张冠李戴】互相引用（cite one another / cite each other）是引用卡特尔中作者群体和期刊群体的做法，并非支持服务咨询机构要求投稿人互引。"}},{"q_num":38,"stem":"The function of the “milk cow“ journals is to","options":{"A":"boost citation counts for certain authors.","B":"help scholars publish articles at low cost.","C":"instruct first-time contributors in citation.","D":"increase the readership of new journals."},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":3,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第3段：“奶牛期刊（milk cows）”每期所有文章都会引用某篇或某系列特定论文，甚至在发表当年就让一篇论文猛增150多次引用，专门用于为特定论文/作者刷高引用量。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第3段指出“milk cow”期刊中一期内的每篇文章都可能引用某特定论文或系列论文（cite a specific paper or a series of papers），使一篇论文同年激增逾150次引用，其核心功能正是为特定作者抬高引用次数（boost citation counts for certain authors）。","B":"【无中生有】原文提到电子出版降低了新办期刊门槛，但并未说“奶牛期刊”的功能是帮学者低成本发表文章（publish articles at low cost）。","C":"【无中生有】第3段完全未提及指导初次投稿者如何引用（instruct first-time contributors）。","D":"【正反混淆】第3段明确指出这类期刊本身并不获利（not profiting at all），只是在为其他期刊提供引用，而非提高自身新期刊的读者量。"}},{"q_num":39,"stem":"What can be learned about Scopus from the last two paragraphs?","options":{"A":"It fosters competition among citation providers.","B":"It has the capability to identify suspicious citations.","C":"It hinders the growth of “international“ journals.","D":"It is established to prevent citation manipulation."},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":5,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位最后两段（第4–5段），尤其是第5段首两句：Scopus本身掌握着检测这种不当行为所需的全部数据（has all the data necessary to detect this malpractice），例如首年引用量激增就是危险信号。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【无中生有】最后两段指出引用操纵在Scopus中猖獗，并未提及Scopus促进引用提供者之间的竞争。","B":"【正解】第5段首句直言“Scopus itself has all the data necessary to detect this malpractice”，并举例说明首年大量引用即预警信号（Red flags），直接对应 It has the capability to identify suspicious citations（有能力识别可疑引用）。","C":"【正反混淆】第4段指出Scopus收录了大量新兴“国际”期刊（includes a high number of the new \"international\" journals），而非阻碍其发展。","D":"【偷换概念】第4段说明Scopus是一个引文数据库（a citation database）且成了引用操纵的靶子，并非专门为防止引用操纵而设立。"}},{"q_num":40,"stem":"What should an author do to deal with citation manipulators?","options":{"A":"Take legal action.","B":"Demand an apology.","C":"Seek professional advice.","D":"Reveal their misconduct."},"answer":"D","hint":{"para":5,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第5段末句：当编辑、审稿人或支持服务机构要求你添加不当参考文献时，切勿照办，并务必向期刊举报该请求（do not oblige and do report the request to the journal）。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【无中生有】末段建议作者拒绝并向期刊举报，并未提及采取法律行动（Take legal action）。","B":"【无中生有】原文未提及要求操纵者道歉（Demand an apology）。","C":"【无中生有】原文要求向期刊举报而非寻求专业建议（Seek professional advice）。","D":"【正解】第5段末句明确建议“do not oblige and do report the request to the journal”，其中“report the request”精准同义替换为 Reveal their misconduct（揭露其不当行为）。"}}],"detailed_analysis":"本文剖析科研论文评价过度依赖期刊影响因子与论文被引次数所引发的学术造假问题。文中依次揭露了期刊/作者互引集团（citation cartels）、建议作者额外添加引用的支持服务咨询机构、专门为他人刷引用的“奶牛期刊（milk cows）”，以及该乱象在Scopus数据库中的泛滥。末段强调Scopus掌握检测违规所需的全部数据，并告诫作者遇到不当加引要求时应拒绝并举报。","keywords":[{"word":"citation","trans":"n. 引用，引证"},{"word":"misconduct","trans":"n. 不端行为，渎职"},{"word":"metric","trans":"n. 度量指标"},{"word":"cartel","trans":"n. 卡特尔，垄断集团"},{"word":"rigorous","trans":"adj. 严格的，严密的"},{"word":"integrity","trans":"n. 正直，学术诚信"}]},{"id":"eng1_2025_t1","exam":"英语一","year":"2025","text_num":"Text 1","title":"莎士比亚排练室教学法助力小学生英语与情感发展","difficulty":"困难★★★★★","summary":"介绍皇家莎士比亚剧团委托开展的随机对照实验：通过让学生在“排练室”中亲身演绎莎剧，不仅显著拓宽了小学生的词汇量与写作表达力，还极大提升了其共情与情感素养。","paragraphs":["The grammar school boy from Stratford-upon-Avon has landed a scholarly punch after ground-breaking research showed that Shakespeare does benefit children’s literacy and emotional development. But only if you act him out.","A study found that a “rehearsal room” approach to teaching Shakespeare broadened children’s vocabulary and the complexity of their writing as well as their emotional literacy. “The research shows that the way actors work makes a big difference to the way children use language and also how they think about themselves,” Jacqui O’Hanlon of the Royal Shakespeare Company (RSC), which commissioned the study, said.","The randomised control trial involved hundreds of year 5 pupils—aged nine and ten—at 45 state primary schools that had not been “previously exposed to RSC pedagogy”. They were split into target and control groups and asked to write, for example, a message in a bottle as Ferdinand after the shipwreck in The Tempest. The target group was given a 30-minute drama-based activity to accompany the passage.","The peer-reviewed results showed that the target group of pupils drew on a wider vocabulary, used words “classed as more sophisticated or rarer”, and wrote at greater length. They also “appear to be more comfortable writing in role...while [control] group imagine how they themselves would react to being shipwrecked, [target] group put themselves in the shoes of a literary character and express that character’s emotion”.","The Time to Act study also found that while control pupils relied on “desert island cliches” such as palm trees, target pupils were “more expansive [giving] a broader picture of the sky, the sea and the atmospheric conditions”.","O’Hanlon said she had been most surprised by the “emotional literacy that was evident in the [target] children’s writing” and that they were “more resilient in their writing, more hopeful”. She added: “The emotional understanding was very evident and it is probably related to the [rehearsal room process] where you are used to trying to imagine your way through. They were comfortable in describing different emotional states and part of what you do in drama is put yourself in different shoes.” The study showed the importance of embedding the arts in education, she said.","But could the results be replicated with any old dramatist? O’Hanlon said more research would be needed but suggested that Shakespeare’s use of 20,000 words, compared with the everyday 2,000 words, gave a “massive expansion of language into children’s lives”, which was combined with children “using their whole bodies to bring words to life”."],"questions":[{"q_num":21,"stem":"The \"rehearsal room\" approach requires pupils to ____.","options":{"A":"rewrite the lines from Shakespeare","B":"watch RSC actors’ performances","C":"play the roles in Shakespeare","D":"study drama under RSC artists"},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":2,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第1–2段及第4段：第1段末句点明“only if you act him out（前提是把他演出来）”，第2段称该排练室方法采用演员的工作方式（the way actors work），第4段提到代入角色（in role / put themselves in the shoes of a literary character）。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偷换概念】第3段是让学生以剧中人物身份写漂流瓶信件作为测评任务，而“排练室”教学法的核心是戏剧表演（act out / drama-based activity），而非改写莎剧台词（rewrite the lines）。","B":"【无中生有】原文强调学生像演员一样亲身演绎（the way actors work），并未要求学生观看RSC演员的演出。","C":"【正解】第1段强调“only if you act him out”，第2段说明该方法借鉴演员工作方式，第4、7段进一步指出学生代入角色并用身体让文字鲜活起来，精准对应 play the roles in Shakespeare。","D":"【偷换概念】皇家莎士比亚剧团（RSC）是委托开展该研究的机构，实验是在45所公立小学内通过30分钟戏剧活动进行的，并非让学生在RSC艺术家手下学习戏剧。"}},{"q_num":22,"stem":"The study divided the pupils into two groups to find whether ____.","options":{"A":"the change in instruction enhances learning outcomes","B":"expanding vocabulary helps develop reading fluency","C":"emotion affects understanding of sophisticated works","D":"the classroom activity stimulates interest in the arts"},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":3,"type":"推理判断题","focus":"定位第3–4段：研究将45所小学五年级学生随机分为实验组和对照组，仅对实验组额外提供30分钟戏剧活动，借此验证教学方式的改变能否提升词汇、写作和情感素养等学习成效。"},"question_type":"推理判断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第3段随机分组的唯一变量是实验组增加了30分钟戏剧排练教学活动（a 30-minute drama-based activity），第4–6段对比了两组在词汇、篇幅、描写与情感素养上的表现，说明分组旨在检验教学方式的改变能否提升学习成果（the change in instruction enhances learning outcomes）。","B":"【偷换概念】词汇量扩大是实验组取得的结果之一，分组并非为了检验“扩大词汇是否有助于提升阅读流畅度（reading fluency）”。","C":"【无中生有】实验考察的是戏剧教学如何促进写作与情感素养，而非考察“情绪如何影响对高深作品的理解”。","D":"【偷换概念】研究评估的是对儿童语言写作与情感理解（literacy and emotional development）的作用，并非检验课堂活动是否激发对艺术的兴趣（interest in the arts）。"}},{"q_num":23,"stem":"Control pupils' reliance on \"desert island cliches\" shows their ____.","options":{"A":"weakness in description","B":"omission of small details","C":"casual style of writing","D":"preference for big words"},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":5,"type":"推理判断题","focus":"定位第5段：对照组依赖棕榈树等“荒岛陈词滥调（desert island cliches）”，而实验组描写则更加开阔丰富（more expansive, giving a broader picture of the sky, the sea and the atmospheric conditions），反衬对照组描写能力较弱。"},"question_type":"推理判断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第5段将对照组与实验组直接对比：对照组停留在棕榈树等“荒岛陈词滥调”，实验组则能更开阔地描绘天空、大海与气候氛围，由此看出对照组在场景描写上较为单薄乏力（weakness in description）。","B":"【偷换概念】对照组的问题在于套用刻板意象、画面局促，而非遗漏细枝末节（omission of small details）。","C":"【无中生有】原文并未评价对照组学生的写作风格随意（casual style of writing）。","D":"【正反混淆】第4段明确指出使用更复杂罕见词汇（more sophisticated or rarer words）的是实验组，而非对照组。"}},{"q_num":24,"stem":"What can promote children’s emotional literacy according to O’Hanlon?","options":{"A":"Writing in an imaginative manner.","B":"Identifying with literary characters.","C":"Drawing inspiration from nature.","D":"Concentrating on real-life situations."},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":6,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第6段：O'Hanlon解释儿童情感理解力的提升源于排练室过程——在戏剧中要设身处地站在不同角色立场上思考（put yourself in different shoes），呼应第4段代入文学角色（put themselves in the shoes of a literary character）。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偷换概念】O'Hanlon虽提到“imagine your way through”，但她紧接着明确点出戏剧活动的关键机制是“put yourself in different shoes（换位代入角色）”，而非笼统的“富有想象力地写作”。","B":"【正解】第6段O'Hanlon明确指出情感素养的显现源于排练室过程，“part of what you do in drama is put yourself in different shoes”，结合第4段“put themselves in the shoes of a literary character and express that character's emotion”，精准对应 Identifying with literary characters（代入/认同文学角色）。","C":"【张冠李戴】第5段描写天空、大海等自然景象是实验组写作丰富度的体现，并非O'Hanlon归因情感素养提升的源头。","D":"【正反混淆】第4、6段均强调代入虚构文学角色去想象，而非聚焦现实生活情境（real-life situations）。"}},{"q_num":25,"stem":"It can be inferred from the last paragraph that ____.","options":{"A":"the new teaching method may work best with Shakespeare","B":"the language of Shakespeare may be formidable for pupils","C":"other old dramatists may be included in primary education","D":"pupils may be reluctant to work on other old dramatists"},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":7,"type":"推断题","focus":"定位第7段：面对“其他古典剧作家能否复制同样效果”的提问，O'Hanlon虽称尚需更多研究，但紧接着强调莎士比亚2万词汇量（相对日常2千词）带来的巨大语言拓展，暗示该教学法用于莎剧可能效果最佳。"},"question_type":"推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第7段先设问“这一成果能否在其他古典剧作家作品上复制？”，O'Hanlon回应虽需更多研究，但特别指出莎士比亚20,000词的庞大词汇量（远超日常2,000词）结合全身表演为儿童带来了巨大的语言拓展，暗示这一新教学法配莎士比亚作品可能效果最佳（may work best with Shakespeare）。","B":"【正反混淆】原文强调莎士比亚庞大词汇量给儿童带来的是“massive expansion of language”，呈积极评价，并未说莎剧语言对小学生令人生畏（formidable）。","C":"【过度推断】O'Hanlon仅表示还需更多研究（more research would be needed），并未推断其他古典剧作家将被纳入小学教育。","D":"【无中生有】末段完全未提及小学生不愿学习其他古典剧作家的作品（reluctant to work on other old dramatists）。"}}],"detailed_analysis":"本文报道了一项关于英国45所公立小学五年级学生的随机对照研究。与仅阅读文本的对照组相比，接受30分钟戏剧排练活动的实验组在写作词汇丰富度、篇幅长度、场景描写广度以及代入文学角色表达情感的能力上均表现更佳。研究者O'Hanlon指出，莎士比亚庞大的2万词库结合全身心表演，使该教学法对儿童读写和情感素养产生了独特助益。","keywords":[{"word":"rehearsal","trans":"n. 排练，演习"},{"word":"literacy","trans":"n. 读写能力，素养"},{"word":"cliche","trans":"n. 陈词滥调"},{"word":"immersive","trans":"adj. 沉浸式的"},{"word":"pedagogical","trans":"adj. 教学法的，教育学的"},{"word":"collaborative","trans":"adj. 合作的，协作的"}]},{"id":"eng1_2025_t2","exam":"英语一","year":"2025","text_num":"Text 2","title":"科研碳排放：人类认知世界的生态代价反思","difficulty":"困难★★★★★","summary":"反驳部分科学家为减少碳排放而主张缩减研究的观点，论证高耗能科研是人类认识世界、追踪气候危机与研发低碳技术（如PERC太阳能电池与负碳超算LUMI）必须付出的长远代价。","paragraphs":["I was shocked to learn recently that some scientists want to scale back their research in an effort to decrease carbon emissions. The crisis is here, they said, and we need to cut back on our energy-intensive modelling. At the very least, we need to make our energy use far more sustainable.","It is unarguable that our laboratories, scientific instruments, rockets and satellites—the tools we scientists need to measure the planet’s pulse—demand significant amounts of energy both in their construction and operation. And it is equally true that science’s unrelenting appetite for information has caused a mushrooming of energy-intensive data centres around the world. According to the International Energy Agency, these buildings now consume about 1 per cent of the world’s electricity.","However, this is a price we must pay for understanding the world. How can we inform decision makers about the best ways to bring down carbon emissions if we can’t track the amount of carbon dioxide in the atmosphere, where it’s coming from and who’s producing it? The carbon emissions from technological research are well spent: ultimately this research will safeguard the future of our planet.","It can be hard for scientists to make the case because our work is complex, often takes place behind closed doors and does not always lend itself to easy interpretation or explanation. But demonstrating the efficacy of science will be crucial if we are to solve humanity’s greatest challenges.","Recognising the hope that science and engineering can bring was the impetus behind the creation of the Millennium Technology Prize, which is now entering its 20th year as a celebration of human ingenuity. One of the past winners, Professor Martin Green from the University of New South Wales, Australia, is the inventor of the Passivated Emitter and Rear Cell technology which is now found in most of the world’s solar panels. Thanks to his invention, we have a real chance to decrease the world’s carbon emissions.","Every day, scientists, technologists and engineers are discovering new ways to exploit renewable energy sources and develop techniques not just to use power more intelligently but to power our intelligence. A great example of this is Europe’s largest supercomputer, LUMI in Finland, which is astonishingly carbon-negative. Established in an old paper mill, it is powered by a nearby river and its remote heat warms the people who live in the surrounding town of Kajaani.","If the world is to meet its net-zero ambitions, we must think hard about how we can deliver sustainable computing and deliver more LUMIs."],"questions":[{"q_num":26,"stem":"The author expressed great surprise at some scientists' ____.","options":{"A":"unwillingness to cut carbon emissions","B":"intention to reduce their research","C":"suspicions about sustainable energy","D":"waste of electricity in their projects"},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":1,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第1段首句：作者直言震惊（I was shocked to learn）——竟然有科学家为了减少碳排放而想要缩减研究规模（want to scale back their research）。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正反混淆】第1段明言这些科学家是“为了减少碳排放（in an effort to decrease carbon emissions）”才想缩减研究，并非不愿减排。","B":"【正解】第1段首句“I was shocked to learn recently that some scientists want to scale back their research...”中，“shocked”对应 great surprise，“want to scale back their research”精准同义替换为 intention to reduce their research。","C":"【正反混淆】第1段末句科学家呼吁让能源使用更具可持续性（make our energy use far more sustainable），并非对可持续能源心存怀疑。","D":"【偷换概念】令作者震惊的是科学家主动缩减研究的意图，而非科研项目“浪费电力（waste of electricity）”。"}},{"q_num":27,"stem":"The author believes that carbon emissions from research ____.","options":{"A":"have caused grave consequences","B":"have aroused groundless worries","C":"are hard to handle at present","D":"are justifiable in the long run"},"answer":"D","hint":{"para":3,"type":"观点态度题","focus":"定位第3段首尾句：作者指出科研耗能是理解世界必须付出的代价（a price we must pay），科研产生的碳排放花得值（are well spent），最终将守护地球未来（ultimately... safeguard the future of our planet）。"},"question_type":"观点态度题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正反混淆】作者明确为科研碳排放辩护，称其“well spent”，而非认为它造成了严重后果（grave consequences）。","B":"【正反混淆】第2段作者以“It is unarguable...”承认科研确实耗能巨大，并非认为相关担忧毫无根据（groundless worries），只是主张不能因此缩减科研。","C":"【无中生有】第3段重在说明科研碳排的必要性与长远价值，并未说目前难以处理（hard to handle at present）；第6段还举了负碳超算LUMI的成功案例。","D":"【正解】第3段末句指出“The carbon emissions from technological research are well spent: ultimately this research will safeguard the future of our planet”，“well spent”和“ultimately”精准对应 are justifiable in the long run（从长远来看是合理正当的）。"}},{"q_num":28,"stem":"The example of Green in Paragraph 5 is used to illustrate ____.","options":{"A":"the achievements of great scientists","B":"the urgency of addressing climate change","C":"the rewards of scientific endeavours","D":"the value of fostering human ingenuity"},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":5,"type":"例证题","focus":"定位第4段末句与第5段：第4段末强调展示科学成效（efficacy of science）至关重要，第5段以千禧技术奖彰显科学与工程带来的希望（hope that science and engineering can bring），并用Martin Green发明PERC太阳能电池使减排成为可能为例，说明科学努力带来的丰硕回报。"},"question_type":"例证题","option_analysis":{"A":"【就事论事】例证题考查例子所服务的论点，A项仅停留在“伟大科学家的成就”这一表层事实，未点出科研回报对解决气候问题的意义。","B":"【答非所问】Green的发明是为了展示科研能带来减排的真正希望与成效，而非论证应对气候变化的紧迫性（urgency）。","C":"【正解】第4段末提出“demonstrating the efficacy of science will be crucial”，第5段承接指出“Recognising the hope that science and engineering can bring”，随即以Green发明PERC太阳能电池技术、让全球真正有机会降低碳排放为例，生动阐明科学探索所带来的实质回报（the rewards of scientific endeavours）。","D":"【偷换概念】第5段仅在定语从句中称千禧技术奖是“celebration of human ingenuity（对人类智慧的礼赞）”，并未讨论“培养（fostering）人类智慧的价值”；Green的事例落脚在“Thanks to his invention, we have a real chance to decrease...”，强调科研成果的回报。"}},{"q_num":29,"stem":"It can be learned from the last two paragraphs that LUMI ____.","options":{"A":"is a model of sustainability efforts","B":"is a triumph against energy shortage","C":"owes much to global net-zero initiatives","D":"aims to explore the power of intelligence"},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":6,"type":"细节推断题","focus":"定位第6–7段：欧洲最大超算LUMI惊人地实现了负碳排放（carbon-negative），依靠河流水电运行并将余热供给周边城镇取暖；第7段呼吁打造更多LUMI以实现可持续计算，说明LUMI是可持续发展努力的典范。"},"question_type":"细节推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第6段将芬兰超算LUMI作为开发可再生能源与智能用电的典范（A great example of this），指出其实现负碳排放（carbon-negative）、采用水电并利用余热为小镇供暖；第7段呼吁建设更多LUMI以实现可持续计算（sustainable computing），精准对应 is a model of sustainability efforts。","B":"【无中生有】最后两段围绕减排与可持续计算展开，并未提及对抗能源短缺（energy shortage）。","C":"【因果倒置】第7段说要实现全球净零目标，我们需要打造更多LUMI，即LUMI助力净零目标，而非LUMI“归功于（owes much to）”全球净零倡议。","D":"【望文生义】第6段“not just to use power more intelligently but to power our intelligence”意为用更环保的电力驱动科研算力/智慧，并非LUMI以“探索智能的力量（explore the power of intelligence）”为目标。"}},{"q_num":30,"stem":"Which of the following statements would the author agree with?","options":{"A":"Emission-free modelling demands extra funding.","B":"The need for supercomputers is difficult to meet.","C":"Energy-intensive research work is inevitable.","D":"The goals of researchers ought to be realistic."},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":3,"type":"观点态度题","focus":"定位第2–3段：作者承认实验室、科研仪器、数据中心等高耗能科研需求无可争辩（unarguable），并指出这是人类理解世界必须付出的代价（a price we must pay），可见作者认同高耗能科研工作不可避免。"},"question_type":"观点态度题","option_analysis":{"A":"【无中生有】全文未提及无排放建模需要额外资金（extra funding）。","B":"【无中生有】原文未提及对超级计算机的需求难以满足（difficult to meet）。","C":"【正解】第2段指出科研工具与数据中心必然消耗大量能源（unarguable... demand significant amounts of energy），第3段明确强调“However, this is a price we must pay for understanding the world”，表明作者认为高耗能科研工作是不可避免且必要的（Energy-intensive research work is inevitable）。","D":"【无中生有】全文并未探讨研究者的目标是否应该切合实际（ought to be realistic）。"}}],"detailed_analysis":"本文针对部分科学家提议缩减高耗能科研建模以减排的现象展开反驳。作者承认实验室、科研仪器、火箭卫星及数据中心消耗了大量能源（数据中心约占全球用电1%），但指出这是理解地球与应对气候危机必须付出的代价，科研碳排物有所值。随后以千禧技术奖得主Martin Green发明PERC太阳能电池技术，以及芬兰负碳排放超算LUMI为例，论证科研探索的丰硕回报与可持续计算的光明前景。","keywords":[{"word":"footprint","trans":"n. 足迹，碳排量"},{"word":"supercomputing","trans":"n. 超级计算"},{"word":"dilemma","trans":"n. 两难困境"},{"word":"sustainability","trans":"n. 可持续性"},{"word":"observatory","trans":"n. 天文台"},{"word":"hypocrisy","trans":"n. 伪善，虚伪"}]},{"id":"eng1_2025_t3","exam":"英语一","year":"2025","text_num":"Text 3","title":"盗版流媒体：好莱坞影视工业面临的新威胁","difficulty":"困难★★★★★","summary":"揭示数字流媒体时代非法盗版流媒体以近90%暴利肆虐的现状，用详实数据展现其对美国及全球经济造成的巨额损失，并梳理美国电影协会（MPA）与ACE执法小组在立法及打击盗版上的进展与长期挑战。","paragraphs":["Ever since taking on Netflix Inc. at its own game, old Hollywood has struggled to turn a profit in streaming, with the likes of Disney+, Peacock and Paramount+ losing billions of dollars each year, sparking concerns on Wall Street that the services will never be as profitable as cable once was. But the age of streaming has been a boon for some unintended winners: pirates that use software to rip a film or television show in seconds from legitimate online video platforms and host the titles on their own, illegitimate services, which rake in about $2 billion annually from ads and subscriptions.","With no video production costs, illegal streaming sites have achieved profit margins approaching 90%, according to the Motion Picture Association (MPA), a trade group representing Hollywood studios that’s working to crack down on the thousands of illegal platforms that have cropped up in recent years.","Initially the rise of legitimate online businesses such as Netflix actually helped curb digital piracy, which had largely been based on file uploads. But now piracy involving illegal streaming services as well as file-sharing costs the US economy about $30 billion in lost revenue a year and some 250,000 jobs, estimates the US Chamber of Commerce’s Global Innovation Policy Center. The global impact is about $71 billion annually.","“The people who are stealing our movies and our television shows and operating piracy sites are not mom and pop operations,” says Charlie Rivkin, chief executive officer of the MPA. “This is organized crime.” Rivkin joined the MPA in 2017 after the organization failed five years earlier to build consensus between Hollywood and Silicon Valley to win passage of legislation in Congress aimed at stopping online piracy. In 2017 the association formed the Alliance for Creativity and Entertainment (ACE), an enforcement task force of about 100 detectives circling the globe to help local authorities arrest streaming pirates.","ACE says it’s helped shrink the number of illegal streaming services in North America to 126, from more than 1,400 in 2018, aided in part by the MPA’s support for a 2020 federal law that made large-scale streaming of copyrighted material a serious crime.","Consulting firm Parks Associates predicts that legitimate US streaming services’ cumulative loss from piracy since 2022 will reach $113 billion in the next two years. “While there is some optimism that emerging countermeasures and best practices may see piracy begin to plateau by 2027, there is no consensus among stakeholders as to when it may begin to decline,” says analyst Steve Hawley."],"questions":[{"q_num":31,"stem":"According to Paragraph 1, legitimate streaming services ____.","options":{"A":"have drawn lessons from Hollywood","B":"have surpassed cable in revenue","C":"are unpopular with advertisers","D":"are confronted with a real threat"},"answer":"D","hint":{"para":1,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第1段：一方面迪士尼+等正规流媒体每年亏损数十亿美元，另一方面盗版者用软件几秒钟就能从正规平台盗录影视作品并借广告和订阅年敛约20亿美元，说明正规流媒体正面临切实威胁。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偷换概念】第1段首句说老牌好莱坞在流媒体领域与Netflix竞争却难以盈利，并非正规流媒体从好莱坞汲取了教训（drawn lessons）。","B":"【正反混淆】第1段指出华尔街担忧流媒体服务永远无法像当年的有线电视那样盈利（never be as profitable as cable once was），而非收入超过有线电视。","C":"【无中生有】第1段提到盗版平台靠广告和订阅牟利，并未说正规流媒体不受广告商欢迎（unpopular with advertisers）。","D":"【正解】第1段后半句指出盗版者使用软件在几秒内从正规在线视频平台盗取影视内容并在非法平台上每年牟利约20亿美元，叠加正规平台连年巨亏的处境，清晰说明正规流媒体正面临实实在在的威胁（are confronted with a real threat）。"}},{"q_num":32,"stem":"It can be learned that streamers like Netflix ____.","options":{"A":"played a part in the fight against illegal file-sharing","B":"reaped benefits from the war with digital pirates","C":"promised to become big job creators in the US","D":"used to collaborate with file-uploading platforms"},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":3,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第3段首句：最初，像Netflix这样的正规在线流媒体兴起，实际上帮助遏制了此前主要依赖文件上传的数字盗版（actually helped curb digital piracy, which had largely been based on file uploads）。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第3段首句明确指出：“Initially the rise of legitimate online businesses such as Netflix actually helped curb digital piracy, which had largely been based on file uploads.”“helped curb”对应 played a part in the fight against，“file uploads”与本段后文“file-sharing”呼应，故A项正确。","B":"【正反混淆】原文说正规流媒体曾遏制盗版，如今又深受非法流媒体盗版之害，并未说其从与数字盗版的战争中获利（reaped benefits）。","C":"【张冠李戴】第3段提到的25万个工作岗位是盗版导致的美国经济损失（costs... some 250,000 jobs），并非Netflix承诺创造大量就业。","D":"【正反混淆】Netflix等正规流媒体是遏制（curb）了以文件上传为主的盗版，而非曾与文件上传平台合作（collaborate）。"}},{"q_num":33,"stem":"It can be inferred from Paragraph 4 that the MPA ____.","options":{"A":"was denied cooperation by Silicon Valley","B":"led a national protest against online piracy","C":"was urged to form an enforcement task force","D":"failed to win support from local authorities"},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":4,"type":"推断题","focus":"定位第4段第三句：Rivkin在2017年加入MPA，而在此五年前MPA未能促使好莱坞与硅谷达成共识以推动国会通过反网络盗版立法（failed... to build consensus between Hollywood and Silicon Valley），可推知MPA遭到了硅谷的拒绝配合。"},"question_type":"推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第4段指出MPA五年前未能在好莱坞与硅谷之间建立共识以推动国会通过打击网络盗版的立法（failed five years earlier to build consensus between Hollywood and Silicon Valley）；MPA代表好莱坞制片厂，未能与硅谷达成共识即意味着未获得硅谷的合作（was denied cooperation by Silicon Valley）。","B":"【偷换概念】MPA推动的是国会立法并组建执法工作组（enforcement task force），而非领导全国性抗议活动（national protest）。","C":"【无中生有】第4段仅陈述“In 2017 the association formed the Alliance for Creativity and Entertainment (ACE)”，并未提及MPA是“被敦促（was urged）”成立该组织的。","D":"【正反混淆】第4段末句指出ACE的约100名侦探奔赴全球“协助地方当局逮捕盗版者（help local authorities arrest streaming pirates）”，并未说未能赢得地方当局支持。"}},{"q_num":34,"stem":"According to Hawley, digital piracy ____.","options":{"A":"cannot be checked in spite of new legislation","B":"will possibly overwhelm legitimate streamers","C":"is unlikely to diminish in the near future","D":"has been underestimated by some analysts"},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":6,"type":"细节推断题","focus":"定位第6段末句：分析师Steve Hawley指出，尽管有人乐观预计到2027年盗版可能开始趋于平稳，但利益相关方对盗版何时开始下降尚无共识（no consensus... as to when it may begin to decline），即短期内不太可能减少。"},"question_type":"细节推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正反混淆】第5段指出在2020年联邦法律助力下，北美非法流媒体服务已从1400多个缩减至126个，说明新立法有一定遏制作用，且Hawley并未说立法完全无效。","B":"【过度推断】Hawley仅表示各方对盗版何时下降尚无共识，并未断言盗版会压倒/击垮正规流媒体（overwhelm legitimate streamers）。","C":"【正解】第6段末句Hawley指出，即便到2027年也仅是乐观预计“begin to plateau（趋于平缓）”，至于何时开始下降各方并无共识（no consensus... as to when it may begin to decline），精准对应 is unlikely to diminish in the near future（短期内不太可能减少）。","D":"【无中生有】Hawley并未提及某些分析师低估了数字盗版（underestimated by some analysts）。"}},{"q_num":35,"stem":"Which of the following is emphasized in the text?","options":{"A":"The need to coordinate anti-piracy action.","B":"The criminal nature of copyright violation.","C":"The prospect of eliminating online piracy.","D":"The economic harm from illegal streaming."},"answer":"D","hint":{"para":3,"type":"主旨要义题","focus":"贯通全文第1、2、3、6段：文章反复列举惊人经济数据——盗版年敛20亿美元、利润率近90%、美国年损300亿美元与25万岗位、全球年损710亿美元、美国正规流媒体累计损失将达1130亿美元，核心突出非法流媒体的巨大经济危害。"},"question_type":"主旨要义题","option_analysis":{"A":"【以偏概全】第4–5段提及MPA和ACE的执法行动，但这仅是应对措施的一部分，并非贯穿全文最强调的核心。","B":"【以偏概全】版权侵犯的犯罪性质（organized crime / serious crime）仅在第4–5段局部提及，无法概括全文反复渲染的损失主线。","C":"【正反混淆】第6段明确指出各方对盗版何时开始下降尚无共识，文章并未强调“消除网络盗版的前景（prospect of eliminating online piracy）”。","D":"【正解】全文多处以具体金额与数据（年敛20亿、利润率近90%、美国年损300亿及25万岗位、全球年损710亿、未来两年累计损失达1130亿）反复凸显非法流媒体带来的惨重经济损失，精准对应 The economic harm from illegal streaming。"}}],"detailed_analysis":"本文聚焦好莱坞正规流媒体面临的盗版危机。老牌制片厂进军流媒体本就连年亏损，非法盗版网站更凭借零制作成本获取近90%利润率，每年给美国经济造成约300亿美元和25万个岗位损失（全球年损710亿美元）。美国电影协会（MPA）虽于2017年组建ACE反盗版执法小组并借助2020年联邦重罪法案大幅削减北美盗版网站，但分析师Steve Hawley指出，盗版何时下降仍无共识，正规流媒体累计损失将继续扩大。","keywords":[{"word":"piracy","trans":"n. 盗版，海盗行为"},{"word":"streaming","trans":"n. 流媒体"},{"word":"infringement","trans":"n. 侵权，违反"},{"word":"subscription","trans":"n. 订阅，订阅费"},{"word":"syndication","trans":"n. 联合分销"},{"word":"enforcement","trans":"n. 执法，执行"}]},{"id":"eng1_2025_t4","exam":"英语一","year":"2025","text_num":"Text 4","title":"数字历史记录保存与软硬件迭代危机","difficulty":"困难★★★★★","summary":"对比有形实体文物与无形数字资料的保存特性，指出数字信息面临创作者忽视、载体与信息分离、技术格式迅速淘汰以及图书馆价值被低估等严峻挑战，强调图书馆员在数字历史保存中的关键作用。","paragraphs":["Visit any antiques store and you’ll encounter artifacts from the past: photographs, letters, a brochure detailing the Sinclair dinosaur exhibit from the 1964-1965 World’s Fair, the ephemera of history. Yet these objects aren’t truly ephemeral, because they’re still here, decades, even centuries later. Why? Because they’re tangible.","Have you pondered the life cycle of intangible formats, digital information, given that those who produce these artifacts seldom make provision for their long-term preservation? For millennia, we’ve known what we’ve known due to artifacts that have survived, often despite their original creators’ neglect. The thing itself is the medium that delivers the information. At the time of creation, no attempts were made at intentional preservation, yet analog materials have a chance of surviving and serving as the historical record that biographers, historians, and novelists rely on. Libraries and archives have traditionally shouldered the responsibility of organization, preservation, and access to information. One of S.R. Ranganathan’s foundational Laws of Library Science is “Save the time of the reader.” Thus, librarians digitize the tangible so that researchers the world over can quickly search and access their holdings. The result is an embarrassment of historical riches, which brings its own needle-and-haystack problems.","Librarians’ selfless devotion can act against us when users point to universality of access by holding up a cellphone and saying, “it’s all in here” as evidence that libraries are less vital for researchers today. Yet how was that universality of access made possible and, perhaps more importantly, how is it maintained? Who curates what is preserved? When it comes to born-digital information, the terrifying answer can be: if not librarians and archivists, then no one. Digital information requires a great deal more care than analog.","Even when a digital object is preserved, it may only be the carrier that’s saved, not the information itself. As technology advances and a format becomes obsolete, the object is useless. Have you ever stared helplessly at a ZIP disk, thinking: how do I get the files off this? Without constant migration of digital assets, a nightmare about the foreseeable future is what keeps historians up at night: a historical record that abruptly stops when digital replaces analog.","As a librarian whose day job revolves around special collections and digital assets, I share the night terrors of historians, and I’d be lying if I said a comprehensive preservation solution currently exists. Yet researchers can take some comfort in the fact that there are a multitude of librarians devoted to discovering, organizing, and preserving digital information for researchers current and future. Librarians are uniquely positioned to understand how end users seek and use information. Thus we play an integral role in identifying, preserving, and providing accessibility to digital artifacts so that, while future researchers may find the digital realm a challenging place to ply their trade, they won’t find it an impossible one."],"questions":[{"q_num":36,"stem":"The author mentions the artifacts from the past to ____.","options":{"A":"introduce the coming of antiques","B":"contrast them with everyday items","C":"bring up the issue of preservation","D":"comment on their historical value"},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":1,"type":"例证/写作目的题","focus":"定位第1段与第2段首句：第1段列举古董店中跨越数十年乃至数百年仍存留的有形文物，第2段首句随即转向反问——数字信息生产者很少为其长期保存（long-term preservation）作安排，可见提及过去文物是为了引出“保存”议题。"},"question_type":"例证/写作目的题","option_analysis":{"A":"【答非所问】提及古董店里的照片、信件只是开篇引子，目的并非介绍“古董的由来（coming of antiques）”。","B":"【张冠李戴】作者是将有形的历史文物与无形的数字信息（intangible formats, digital information）对比，而非与日常用品（everyday items）对比。","C":"【正解】第1段先展示有形旧物得以跨越世纪留存，第2段首句紧接着追问无形数字信息的生命周期——“given that those who produce these artifacts seldom make provision for their long-term preservation”，显然是为了引出信息保存问题（bring up the issue of preservation）。","D":"【答非所问】第1段强调这些旧物“依然存在（still here）因为它们是有形的（tangible）”，并未评论其历史价值的高低。"}},{"q_num":37,"stem":"Compared with digital objects, tangible artifacts ____.","options":{"A":"are less subject to their creators’ neglect","B":"convey information in a more direct way","C":"require more intentional preservation","D":"are less likely to suffer serious damage"},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":2,"type":"细节推断题","focus":"定位第2段第三句并结合第4段对比：第2段指出实体文物“本身就是传递信息的媒介（The thing itself is the medium that delivers the information）”；而第4段指出数字对象的载体与信息分离，格式过时就无法读取。故实体文物传递信息更直接。"},"question_type":"细节推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偷换概念/正反混淆】第2段指出实体文物是在“往往遭到原作者忽视（often despite their original creators' neglect）”且“创作时未尝试刻意保存”的情况下幸存的，它们同样遭受了创作者忽视，并非“更少遭受创作者忽视”。","B":"【正解】第2段明确说明对于有形文物，“The thing itself is the medium that delivers the information”（物体本身就是传递信息的媒介），无需依赖额外软硬件解码；与之对比，第4段指出数字对象往往“仅保存了载体而非信息本身（only be the carrier that's saved, not the information itself）”，格式淘汰便成废品。因此有形文物以更直接的方式传递信息（convey information in a more direct way）。","C":"【正反混淆】第2段称有形模拟材料创作时并未试图刻意保存（no attempts were made at intentional preservation），第3段更直言数字信息比模拟材料需要多得多的照料（requires a great deal more care than analog），C项与原文完全相反。","D":"【无中生有】原文比较的是保存机制与可读性（有形vs无形、格式过时），并未比较两者遭受严重物理损坏的概率。"}},{"q_num":38,"stem":"According to Paragraph 3, librarians' work may result in ____.","options":{"A":"oversupply of materials","B":"undervaluation of libraries","C":"researchers’ underperformance","D":"users’ overreliance on technology"},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":3,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第3段首句：图书馆员的无私奉献反而可能适得其反——当用户举起手机说“全都在这里面”并以此证明图书馆对当今研究者不再那么重要（less vital）时，图书馆的价值就被低估了。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偷换概念】第2段末句的“embarrassment of historical riches”指海量数字化史料带来检索难题（大海捞针），属于第2段内容，且并非“材料供应过剩（oversupply）”。","B":"【正解】第3段首句指出：“Librarians' selfless devotion can act against us when users point to universality of access by holding up a cellphone and saying, 'it's all in here' as evidence that libraries are less vital for researchers today.”认为图书馆“不那么重要（less vital）”精准对应 undervaluation of libraries（图书馆价值被低估）。","C":"【无中生有】第3段并未提及研究人员表现不佳（researchers' underperformance）。","D":"【偷换概念】用户举起手机是用来质疑图书馆的重要性，第3段落脚点在于对图书馆价值的误判，而非指责用户过度依赖技术（overreliance on technology）。"}},{"q_num":39,"stem":"The \"ZIP disk\" is cited as an example to show ____.","options":{"A":"the difficulty of retrieving files through unusual means","B":"the infeasibility of constantly migrating digital assets","C":"the possibility of losing information in obsolete formats","D":"the inconvenience of storing information on analog devices"},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":4,"type":"例证题","focus":"定位第4段前三句：先提出论点——随着技术进步和格式过时，数字载体虽存但沦为无用之物（As technology advances and a format becomes obsolete, the object is useless），紧接着举ZIP磁盘无法读取文件的例子来印证过时格式会导致信息丢失风险。"},"question_type":"例证题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偷换概念】ZIP磁盘读不出文件的根源是存储格式过时淘汰，而非“通过不寻常手段检索文件的困难（through unusual means）”。","B":"【正反混淆】第4段末句强调若不持续迁移数字资产（Without constant migration）就会酿成历史断档的噩梦，旨在强调持续迁移的必要性，而非说迁移“不可行（infeasibility）”。","C":"【正解】第4段先指出“Even when a digital object is preserved, it may only be the carrier that's saved, not the information itself. As technology advances and a format becomes obsolete, the object is useless”，随即以对着ZIP磁盘束手无策为例，直接说明信息可能因格式过时而丢失（the possibility of losing information in obsolete formats）。","D":"【张冠李戴】ZIP磁盘是数字存储介质（digital object），而非模拟设备（analog devices）。"}},{"q_num":40,"stem":"Which of the following statements best summarizes the text?","options":{"A":"Hard work should be done to preserve artifacts.","B":"Contributions of librarians should be recognized.","C":"Accessing databases is essential to researchers.","D":"Keeping digital historical records is a challenge."},"answer":"D","hint":{"para":5,"type":"主旨大意题","focus":"纵观全文：第1段引出保存话题，第2–4段层层剖析数字档案保存面临的忽视、维护难、格式过时等困境，第5段作者坦言目前尚无全面解决方案、未来研究者将面对充满挑战的数字领域，主旨即保存数字历史记录极具挑战。"},"question_type":"主旨大意题","option_analysis":{"A":"【范围过宽/偏离核心】仅泛泛谈论“保护文物（preserve artifacts）”，漏掉了全文核心限定对象——数字历史记录（digital）。","B":"【以偏概全】图书馆员的贡献主要在第3、5段体现，是支撑性内容而非贯穿全文的中心主题。","C":"【以偏概全】访问数据库仅是第2段末尾的一个细节，远不能概括全文主旨。","D":"【正解】全文围绕数字信息相比实体文物难以长期保存的困境展开（创作者忽视、格式淘汰、需持续迁移、尚无完善方案），第5段末句亦点出数字领域充满挑战（a challenging place），故 Keeping digital historical records is a challenge 最全面精准地概括了全文主旨。"}}],"detailed_analysis":"本文从古董店里历经数百年依然留存的实体文物切入，引出无形数字信息难以长期保存的核心困境。实体文物本身即传递信息的媒介，即便未经刻意保护也往往得以存续；而数字档案不仅容易因软硬件和格式过时（如ZIP磁盘无法读取）而失效，还因为图书馆员默默将其数字化、让人用手机即可随时查阅，反倒令公众低估图书馆的重要性。作者身为数字资产图书馆员，呼吁正视数字保存的艰巨挑战并肯定图书馆员的不可替代作用。","keywords":[{"word":"artifact","trans":"n. 人工制品，历史遗物"},{"word":"obsolescence","trans":"n. 淘汰，过时"},{"word":"preservation","trans":"n. 保护，保存"},{"word":"tangible","trans":"adj. 有形的，实质的"},{"word":"longevity","trans":"n. 寿命，持久性"},{"word":"archive","trans":"n./v. 档案，归档"}]},{"id":"eng2_2021_t3","exam":"英语二","year":"2021","text_num":"Text 3","title":"微软收购后的“杀手兼并”反垄断策略","difficulty":"偏难★★★★","summary":"以微软2015年收购Wunderlist和Sunrise两款热门应用后将其关停并吸纳工程师为例，剖析科技巨头“买后即杀”式小额收购引发的反垄断担忧，以及美国联邦贸易委员会（FTC）对此展开的调查。","paragraphs":["When Microsoft bought task management app Wunderlist and mobile calendar Sunrise in 2015, it picked two newcomers that were attracting considerable buzz in Silicon Valley. Microsoft's own Office dominates the market for \" productivity \" software, but the start-ups represented a new wave of technology designed from the ground up for the smartphone world.","Both apps, however, were later scrapped, after Microsoft said it had used their best features in its own products. Their teams of engineers stayed on, making them two of the many \"acqui-hires\" that the biggest companies have used to feed their great hunger for tech talent.","To Microsoft's critics, the fates of Wunderlist and Sunrise are examples of a remorseless drive by Big Tech to chew up any innovative companies that lie in their path. \"They bought the seedlings and closed them down,\" complained Paul Arnold, a partner at San Francisco-based Switch Ventures, putting an end to businesses that might one day turn into competitors. Microsoft declined to comment.","Like other start-up investors, Mr. Arnold's own business often depends on selling start-ups to larger tech companies, though he admits to mixed feelings about the result: \"I think these things are good for me, if I put my selfish hat on. But are they good for the American economy? I don't know.\"","The US Federal Trade Commission says it wants to find the answer to that question. This week, it asked the five most valuable US tech companies for information about their many small acquisitions over the past decade. Although only a research project at this stage, the request has raised the prospect of regulators wading into early- stage tech markets that until now have been beyond their reach.","Given their combined market value of more than $5.5 trillion, rifling through such small deals-many of them much less prominent than Wunderlist and Sunrise-might seem beside the point. Between them, the five biggest tech companies have spent an average of only $3.4 billion a year on sub-$1 billion acquisitions over the past five years-a drop in the ocean compared with their massive financial reserves, and the more than $130 billion of venture capital that was invested in the US last year.","However, critics say the big companies use such deals to buy their most threatening potential competitors before their businesses have a chance to gain momentum, in some cases as part of a \"buy and kill\" tactic to simply close them down."],"questions":[{"q_num":31,"stem":"What is true about Wunderlist and Sunrise after their acquisitions?","options":{"A":"Their engineers were retained.","B":"Their market values declined.","C":"Their tech features improved.","D":"Their products were re-priced."},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":2,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第2段第二句：Wunderlist和Sunrise两款应用后来虽被关停（scrapped），但它们的工程师团队留了下来（Their teams of engineers stayed on），即工程师被留用（retained）。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第2段明确指出：“Both apps, however, were later scrapped... Their teams of engineers stayed on, making them two of the many 'acqui-hires'...”其中“stayed on（留下来）”精准同义替换为 were retained，故 Their engineers were retained 正确。","B":"【无中生有】第2段只说两款应用被废弃关停（scrapped），文中并未提及其被收购后“市场价值下降（market values declined）”。","C":"【偷换概念】第2段称微软将两款应用的最佳功能整合进了“微软自家产品（its own products）”，而非这两款被关停的应用自身技术特性得到提升。","D":"【无中生有】原文完全未提及这两款产品被重新定价（re-priced）。"}},{"q_num":32,"stem":"Microsoft's critics believe that the big tech companies tend to ____.","options":{"A":"exaggerate their product quality","B":"eliminate their potential competitors","C":"treat new tech talent unfairly","D":"ignore public opinions"},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":3,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第3段：微软的批评者认为，大科技公司冷酷吞并挡路的创新企业（chew up any innovative companies），买下幼苗再关闭，终结日后可能成为竞争对手的企业（putting an end to businesses that might one day turn into competitors）。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【无中生有】批评者针对的是巨头吞并初创公司的反竞争行为，并未指责其夸大产品质量（exaggerate their product quality）。","B":"【正解】第3段指出批评者认为科技巨头无情吞并创新企业，“putting an end to businesses that might one day turn into competitors”，末段亦重申巨头借此买下最具威胁的潜在对手并关闭（buy and kill），精准对应 eliminate their potential competitors。","C":"【无中生有】第2段提到大公司通过“人才收购（acqui-hires）”满足对技术人才的渴求，并未提及不公正对待新技术人才（treat new tech talent unfairly）。","D":"【无中生有】第3段只说微软拒绝置评（declined to comment），批评者并未声称科技巨头普遍无视公众意见（ignore public opinions）。"}},{"q_num":33,"stem":"Paul Arnold is concerned that small acquisitions might ____.","options":{"A":"weaken big tech companies","B":"worsen market competition","C":"harm the national economy","D":"discourage start-up investors"},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":4,"type":"细节推断题","focus":"定位第4段末两句：风投合伙人Paul Arnold坦言，若从自私角度看把初创公司卖给大厂对自己有利，但随即质疑：“But are they good for the American economy? I don't know.”可见他担忧小额收购损害美国国家经济。"},"question_type":"细节推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正反混淆】科技巨头通过小额收购吸纳人才、消灭潜在对手，增强而非削弱（weaken）自身实力。","B":"【偷换概念】第3段Arnold抱怨巨头买下幼苗并关闭，而第4段他直接表达的深层疑虑落脚在“are they good for the American economy? I don't know”，C项与原文对应最精准直接。","C":"【正解】第4段Paul Arnold坦言卖掉初创企业对自己个人有利，但质疑“But are they good for the American economy? I don't know”，其中“the American economy”精准对应 the national economy，可见他担忧这类收购会损害国家经济（harm the national economy）。","D":"【正反混淆】Arnold本人就是初创企业投资者，他直言“these things are good for me, if I put my selfish hat on”，说明小额收购让投资人获利，而非令其气馁（discourage start-up investors）。"}},{"q_num":34,"stem":"The US Federal Trade Commission intends to ____.","options":{"A":"limit Big Tech's expansion","B":"encourage research collaboration","C":"examine small acquisitions","D":"supervise start-ups' operation"},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":5,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第5段：FTC要求美国市值最高的五家科技公司提交过去十年诸多小额收购的相关信息（asked... for information about their many small acquisitions），并明确说明现阶段仅为一个研究调查项目（only a research project at this stage）。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【过度推断】第5段明确限定FTC目前“仅处于研究项目阶段（only a research project at this stage）”，尚未采取限制大科技公司扩张的强制措施。","B":"【无中生有】第5段说FTC开展的是一项监管研究（research project），并非鼓励科研合作（encourage research collaboration）。","C":"【正解】第5段指出FTC为了弄清小额收购对美国经济的影响，本周已要求五大科技巨头提供过去十年小额收购的信息（asked... for information about their many small acquisitions），精准对应 examine small acquisitions（审查/调查小额收购）。","D":"【偷换概念】FTC收集的是五大科技巨头的并购交易信息，而非监管初创企业的日常运营（supervise start-ups' operation）。"}},{"q_num":35,"stem":"For the five biggest tech companies, their small acquisitions have ____.","options":{"A":"brought little financial pressure","B":"raised few management challenges","C":"set an example for future deals","D":"generated considerable profits"},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":6,"type":"细节推断题","focus":"定位第6段第二句：五大科技巨头过去五年每年在10亿美元以下收购上平均仅花费34亿美元，与其庞大的资金储备相比不过是沧海一粟（a drop in the ocean compared with their massive financial reserves），几乎未带来财务压力。"},"question_type":"细节推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第6段指出，五大科技巨头总市值逾5.5万亿美元，过去五年用于10亿美元以下小额收购的年均支出仅34亿美元，相对其巨额资金储备只是“沧海一粟（a drop in the ocean compared with their massive financial reserves）”，精准对应 brought little financial pressure（几乎未带来财务压力）。","B":"【无中生有】第6段完全聚焦收购金额与资金储备的财务对比，未讨论任何管理挑战（management challenges）。","C":"【无中生有】原文并未说这些小额收购为未来交易树立了榜样（set an example for future deals）。","D":"【无中生有】第6段只强调这些收购的支出相对于巨头财力微不足道，并未提及它们带来了可观利润（generated considerable profits）。"}}],"detailed_analysis":"本文围绕科技巨头针对初创企业的小额收购展开。微软收购任务管理软件Wunderlist和日历应用Sunrise后，在吸收其精华功能并留用工程师团队（“人才收购”）后将两款应用关停。批评者将此视为大科技公司扼杀潜在竞争对手的“买后即杀”策略；风险投资人Paul Arnold则坦言这对自身有利，但担忧是否损害美国经济。为此，美国联邦贸易委员会（FTC）要求五大科技巨头提交过去十年的小额收购信息以展开研究审查。","keywords":[{"word":"acquisition","trans":"n. 收购，兼并"},{"word":"buzz","trans":"n. 热议，轰动"},{"word":"antitrust","trans":"adj. 反垄断的"},{"word":"killer acquisition","trans":"n. 杀手兼并"},{"word":"entrench","trans":"v. 牢固确立，巩固"},{"word":"disruptive","trans":"adj. 颠覆性的"}]},{"id":"eng2_2021_t4","exam":"英语二","year":"2021","text_num":"Text 4","title":"第一印象与薄片认知理论（Nalini Ambady 研究）","difficulty":"偏难★★★★","summary":"介绍心理学家Nalini Ambady的“薄片判断（thin slicing）”等系列实证研究，指出在识人、辨谎与复杂决策时，第一印象与直觉往往优于过度理性分析，但直觉亦存在适用边界，会干扰需要逻辑反思的任务。","paragraphs":["We're fairly good at judging people based on first impressions, thin slices of experience ranging from a glimpse of a photo to five-minute interaction, and deliberation can be not only extraneous but intrusive. In one study of the ability she called \"thin slicing,\" the late psychologist Nalini Ambady asked participants to watch silent 10-second video clips of professors and to rate the instructor's overall effectiveness. Their ratings correlated strongly with students' end-of-semester ratings. Another set of participants had to count backward from 1,000 by nines as they watched the clips, occupying their conscious working memory. Their ratings were just as accurate, demonstrating the intuitive nature of the social processing.","Critically, another group was asked to spend a minute writing down reasons for their judgment, before giving the rating. Accuracy dropped dramatically. Ambady suspected that deliberation focused them on vivid but misleading cues, such as certain gestures or utterances, rather than letting the complex interplay of subtle signals form a holistic impression. She found similar interference when participants watched 15-second clips of pairs of people and judged whether they were strangers, friends, or dating partners.","Other research shows we're better at detecting deception from thin slices when we rely on intuition instead of reflection. \"It's as if you're driving a stick shift,\" says Judith Hall, a psychologist at Northeastern University, \"and if you start thinking about it too much, you can't remember what you're doing. But if you go on automatic pilot, you're fine. Much of our social life is like that.\"","Thinking too much can also harm our ability to form preferences. College students' ratings of strawberry jams and college courses aligned better with experts' opinions when the students weren't asked to analyze their rationale. And people made car-buying decisions that were both objectively better and more personally satisfying when asked to focus on their feelings rather than on details, but only if the decision was complex- when they had a lot of information to process.","Intuition's special powers are unleashed only in certain circumstances. In one study, participants completed a battery of eight tasks, including four that tapped reflective thinking (discerning rules, comprehending vocabulary) and four that tapped intuition and creativity (generating new products or figures of speech). Then they rated the degree to which they had used intuition (\"gut feelings,\" \"hunches,\" \"my heart\"). Use of their gut hurt their performance on the first four tasks, as expected, and helped them on the rest. Sometimes the heart is smarter than the head."],"questions":[{"q_num":36,"stem":"Nalini Ambady's study deals with ____.","options":{"A":"the power of people's memory","B":"the reliability of first impressions","C":"instructor-student interaction","D":"people's ability to influence others"},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":1,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第1段：首句点明人们很擅长凭第一印象（薄片经验）判断他人，紧接着以Ambady的“thin slicing”研究为例，验证仅看10秒无声视频的直觉评分与期末评价高度相关，即探讨第一印象的可靠性。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偷换概念】第1段提到让另一组受试者倒数数字以占用工作记忆（working memory），只是为了检验社交判断的直觉属性，并非研究记忆力的强大。","B":"【正解】第1段首句即点题“We're fairly good at judging people based on first impressions, thin slices of experience”，随后介绍Ambady关于“thin slicing”的研究证明短暂第一印象的评分与学期末评价高度一致，精准对应 the reliability of first impressions。","C":"【以偏概全】评价教授教学效果只是Ambady实验采用的一个场景，研究主题并非“师生互动（instructor-student interaction）”。","D":"【无中生有】第1段研究的是判断他人，而非“影响他人的能力（ability to influence others）”。"}},{"q_num":37,"stem":"In Ambady's study, rating accuracy dropped when participants ____.","options":{"A":"focused on specific details","B":"gave the rating in limited time","C":"watched shorter video clips","D":"discussed with one another"},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":2,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第2段前三句：当另一组受试者在评分前花一分钟写下判断理由时，准确率骤降；Ambady推测，深思使他们聚焦于某些生动却易误导的具体线索（vivid but misleading cues, such as certain gestures or utterances），而非形成整体印象。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第2段指出，让受试者写下理由后准确率大幅下降，因为深思熟虑使他们专注于某些具体却易误导的线索，如特定手势或话语（focused them on vivid but misleading cues, such as certain gestures or utterances），而非形成整体印象，精准对应 focused on specific details。","B":"【偷换概念】第2段提到受试者花一分钟写理由，准确率下降的原因是写理由引发的过度审思，而非“在有限时间内打分（in limited time）”。","C":"【正反混淆】第1段看10秒短片依然准确，第2段看15秒片段同样出现审思干扰，准确率下降并非因为“观看了更短的视频片段”。","D":"【无中生有】实验中受试者是独立写下理由，并未提及彼此讨论（discussed with one another）。"}},{"q_num":38,"stem":"Judith Hall mentions driving to show that ____.","options":{"A":"reflection can be distracting","B":"memory may be selective","C":"social skills must be cultivated","D":"deception is difficult to detect"},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":3,"type":"例证题","focus":"定位第3段：首句论点指出依赖直觉而非反思（intuition instead of reflection）更能识破谎言；随后Judith Hall以开手动挡为例——如果过度思考自己在做什么反而会忘掉动作，说明反思会分散注意力、干扰操作。"},"question_type":"例证题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第3段先提出依赖直觉而非反思（reflection）效果更好，紧接着Judith Hall以驾驶手动挡类比：“if you start thinking about it too much, you can't remember what you're doing. But if you go on automatic pilot, you're fine”，形象说明过度反思会分散干扰注意力（reflection can be distracting）。","B":"【望文生义】虽然类比中出现“can't remember”，但意在说明过度思考会打乱熟练动作，并非论述“记忆具有选择性（memory may be selective）”。","C":"【无中生有】该类比用于解释社交生活中的直觉自动化机制，并未主张“社交技能必须后天培养”。","D":"【偷换概念】虽然第3段首句提到识破欺骗，但开手动挡的类比旨在论证“反思会带来干扰”，而非强调“欺骗很难察觉”。"}},{"q_num":39,"stem":"When you are making complex decisions, it is advisable to ____.","options":{"A":"collect enough data","B":"list your preferences","C":"seek expert advice","D":"follow your feelings"},"answer":"D","hint":{"para":4,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第4段末句：在需要处理大量信息的复杂决策（如买车）中，被要求关注自身感受而非细节的人（asked to focus on their feelings rather than on details），做出的决定既客观更优又更令自己满意。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偷换概念】第4段末句说明复杂决策本身就包含大量信息（a lot of information to process），作者建议的是关注直觉感受，而非去“收集足够的数据”。","B":"【正反混淆】第4段指出大学生不分析理由时评分更接近专家，购车时不纠结细节反而决定更好，列出偏好清单（list your preferences）恰与原文建议相反。","C":"【无中生有】第4段仅用专家意见作为衡量大学生评分准确性的参照标准，并未建议人们做复杂决策时寻求专家建议。","D":"【正解】第4段末句指出，当面临信息繁杂的复杂决策时，关注感受而非细节（focus on their feelings rather than on details）能做出客观更好、主观更满意的决定，精准对应 follow your feelings。"}},{"q_num":40,"stem":"What can we learn from the last paragraph?","options":{"A":"Generating new products takes time.","B":"Intuition may affect reflective tasks.","C":"Vocabulary comprehension needs creativity.","D":"Objective thinking may boost intuitiveness."},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":5,"type":"细节推断题","focus":"定位第5段：实验包含四项反思型任务（推理规律、理解词汇）和四项直觉创意任务，结果显示依赖直觉损害了受试者在前四项反思任务上的表现（Use of their gut hurt their performance on the first four tasks），即直觉会影响反思型任务。"},"question_type":"细节推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【无中生有】末段仅将“构思新产品（generating new products）”列为直觉创意类任务之一，并未提及它需要时间。","B":"【正解】第5段指出，四项任务考查反思思维（reflective thinking），结果受试者动用直觉损害了他们在这四项任务上的表现（Use of their gut hurt their performance on the first four tasks），精准对应 Intuition may affect reflective tasks（直觉可能影响反思性任务）。","C":"【张冠李戴】第5段明确将词汇理解（comprehending vocabulary）归入反思思维任务，而非需要创造力（creativity）的直觉任务。","D":"【无中生有】末段讨论的是直觉对两类任务的正负影响，并未提及“客观思维能增强直觉能力（boost intuitiveness）”。"}}],"detailed_analysis":"本文探讨人类直觉与第一印象的力量及边界。心理学家Nalini Ambady的实验表明，受试者仅凭10秒无声视频对教授的直觉评分便与期末评教高度吻合，而要求写下判断理由（过度深思）反而使准确率暴跌。文章进一步以手动挡驾驶类比说明过度反思的干扰，并指出购车等复杂决策中追随感受更优；但末段通过八项任务实验强调直觉并非万能——它在创意任务中大放异彩，却会损害规律推理、词汇理解等反思性任务。","keywords":[{"word":"thin slice","trans":"n. 薄片，微量行为切片"},{"word":"glimpse","trans":"n./v. 一瞥，短暂感受"},{"word":"unconscious","trans":"adj. 潜意识的，无意识的"},{"word":"intuition","trans":"n. 直觉，第六感"},{"word":"deliberation","trans":"n. 审思，深思熟虑"},{"word":"malpractice","trans":"n. 医疗事故，玩忽职守"}]},{"id":"eng2_2022_t3","exam":"英语二","year":"2022","text_num":"Text 3","title":"商业与网站中误导用户的“暗模式”隐私陷阱","difficulty":"偏难★★★★","summary":"介绍界面设计中操纵用户决策的“暗模式（Dark Patterns）”及其普遍现状，探讨企业内部跨部门协作防欺骗的路径，并结合加州CCPA新规强调行业自律与企业问责的关键作用。","paragraphs":["We have all encountered them, in both our personal and professional lives. Think about the times you felt tricked or frustrated by a membership or subscription that had a seamless sign-up process but was later difficult to cancel. Something that should be simple and transparent can be complicated, intentionally or unintentionally, in ways that impair consumer choice. These are examples of dark patterns.","First coined in 2010 by user experience expert Harry Brignull, \"dark patterns\" is a catch-all term for practices that manipulate user interfaces to influence the decision-making ability of users. Brignull identifies 12 types of common dark patterns, ranging from misdirection and hidden costs to \"roach motel,\" where a user experience seems easy and intuitive at the start, but turns difficult when the user tries to get out.","In a 2019 study of 53,000 product pages and 11,000 websites, researchers found that about one in 10 employs these design practices. Though widely prevalent, the concept of dark patterns is still not well understood. Business and nonprofit leaders should be aware of dark patterns and try to avoid the gray areas they engender.","Where is the line between ethical, persuasive design and dark patterns? Businesses should engage in conversations with IT, compliance, risk, and legal teams to review their privacy policy, and include in the discussion the customer/user experience designers and coders responsible for the company's user interface, as well as the marketers and advertisers responsible for sign-ups, checkout baskets, pricing, and promotions. Any or all these teams can play a role in creating or avoiding \"digital deception.\"","Lawmakers and regulators are slowly starting to address the ambiguity around dark patterns, most recently at the state level. In March, the California Attorney General announced the approval of additional regulations under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) that \"ensure that consumers will not be confused or misled when seeking to exercise their data privacy rights.\" The regulations aim to ban dark patterns- this means prohibiting companies from using confusing language or unnecessary steps such as forcing them to click through multiple screens or listen to reasons why they shouldn't opt out.\"","As more states consider promulgating additional regulations, there is a need for greater accountability from within the business community. Dark patterns also can be addressed on a self-regulatory basis, but only if organizations hold themselves accountable, not just to legal requirements but also to industry best practices and standards."],"questions":[{"q_num":31,"stem":"It can be learned from the first two paragraphs that dark patterns ____.","options":{"A":"improve user experiences","B":"leak user information for profit","C":"undermine users' decision-making","D":"remind users of hidden costs"},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":2,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第1段末两句及第2段首句：暗模式以损害消费者选择（impair consumer choice）的方式把简单流程复杂化，被定义为操纵用户界面以影响用户决策能力（manipulate user interfaces to influence the decision-making ability of users）的做法。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正反混淆】第1段称暗模式让用户感到受骗和沮丧（tricked or frustrated）、损害消费者选择，与“改善用户体验”完全相反。","B":"【无中生有】前两段谈的是难以取消订阅、误导和隐藏费用等操纵界面的手段，并未提及“为牟利泄露用户信息”。","C":"【正解】第1段指出暗模式损害消费者选择（impair consumer choice），第2段首句将其界定为操纵用户界面以影响用户决策能力（manipulate user interfaces to influence the decision-making ability of users），精准对应 undermine users' decision-making。","D":"【正反混淆】第2段指出“隐藏费用（hidden costs）”正是暗模式的常见类型之一，暗模式是隐瞒而非“提醒（remind）”用户注意隐藏费用。"}},{"q_num":32,"stem":"The 2019 study on dark patterns is mentioned to show ____.","options":{"A":"their major flaws","B":"their complex designs","C":"their severe damage","D":"their strong presence"},"answer":"D","hint":{"para":3,"type":"例证题","focus":"定位第3段前两句：研究调查5.3万个商品页和1.1万个网站后发现约十分之一采用暗模式，紧接着以“Though widely prevalent（尽管广泛盛行）”点明该研究意在说明暗模式普遍存在。"},"question_type":"例证题","option_analysis":{"A":"【答非所问】2019年研究给出的是采用暗模式的网站比例（about one in 10），旨在说明其普遍性，而非揭示暗模式自身的“重大缺陷（major flaws）”。","B":"【无中生有】第3段并未借助该研究说明暗模式设计有多复杂（complex designs）。","C":"【无中生有】该研究仅统计了使用占比，并未评估其造成的危害程度（severe damage）。","D":"【正解】第3段首句称约十分之一的网站使用暗模式，次句直接总结为“Though widely prevalent（尽管广泛盛行）”，精准对应 their strong presence（广泛存在）。"}},{"q_num":33,"stem":"To handle digital deception, businesses should ____.","options":{"A":"listen to customer feedback","B":"talk with relevant teams","C":"turn to independent agencies","D":"rely on professional training"},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":4,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第4段：为防范数字欺骗，企业应与IT、合规、风控和法务团队沟通（engage in conversations with...），并把负责界面的设计师、程序员以及负责营销促销的团队纳入讨论。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【无中生有】第4段强调的是企业内部各相关职能团队之间的沟通协作，并未提及倾听顾客反馈（customer feedback）。","B":"【正解】第4段明确建议企业“engage in conversations with IT, compliance, risk, and legal teams... and include in the discussion the customer/user experience designers and coders... as well as the marketers and advertisers”，精准同义替换为 talk with relevant teams（与相关团队沟通）。","C":"【无中生有】文中建议企业内部多部门协同审查，并未提及求助外部独立机构（independent agencies）。","D":"【无中生有】第4段未提及依靠专业培训（professional training）。"}},{"q_num":34,"stem":"The additional regulations under the CCPA are intended to ____.","options":{"A":"guide users through opt-out processes","B":"protect consumers from being tricked","C":"grant companies data privacy rights","D":"restrict access to problematic content"},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":5,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第5段第二句：加州总检察长批准的CCPA附加法规旨在确保消费者在行使数据隐私权时不会被迷惑或误导（ensure that consumers will not be confused or misled），即防止消费者受骗。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偷换概念】第5段指出法规禁止企业用繁琐步骤强迫用户多次点击或听取劝阻理由来阻挠退出，并非“引导用户走完退出流程（guide users through opt-out processes）”。","B":"【正解】第5段直接引用法规宗旨：“ensure that consumers will not be confused or misled when seeking to exercise their data privacy rights”，禁止使用令人困惑的措辞或多余步骤，精准对应 protect consumers from being tricked（保护消费者免受欺骗）。","C":"【张冠李戴】CCPA保障的是消费者（consumers）的数据隐私权，而非授予企业（companies）数据隐私权。","D":"【无中生有】法规打击的是欺骗性界面设计，而非限制获取有问题的内容（problematic content）。"}},{"q_num":35,"stem":"According to the last paragraph, a key to coping with dark patterns is ____.","options":{"A":"new legal requirements","B":"businesses' self-discipline","C":"strict regulatory standards","D":"consumers' safety awareness"},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":6,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第6段：末段强调商业界内部需要更强的问责意识（greater accountability from within the business community），在自律基础上（on a self-regulatory basis）不仅遵守法律，更要恪守行业最佳实践与标准。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【以偏概全】第6段指出组织不仅要遵守法律要求（not just to legal requirements），更要实现内部自律和遵循行业最佳实践，新法律并非末段强调的关键。","B":"【正解】第6段明确指出需要“greater accountability from within the business community”，并称暗模式可通过自律解决（on a self-regulatory basis），前提是企业自我问责（hold themselves accountable），精准对应 businesses' self-discipline（企业自律）。","C":"【偷换概念】末段强调的是“self-regulatory（自律）”与企业内部担当，而非外部的“严格监管标准（strict regulatory standards）”。","D":"【无中生有】末段完全未提及消费者的安全意识（consumers' safety awareness）。"}}],"detailed_analysis":"本文聚焦互联网产品中常见的“暗模式（Dark Patterns）”——即通过操纵用户界面来误导消费者决策的设计手法（如注册顺畅却极难取消的“蟑螂屋”模式）。2019年一项研究揭示约十分之一的网站使用此类设计。作者建议企业召集IT、合规、法务、设计及营销团队共同审查隐私政策与交互界面，避免数字欺骗；在介绍加州CCPA出台禁令后，末段强调除外部立法外，企业自律与遵守行业最佳实践同样是破解暗模式的关键。","keywords":[{"word":"dark pattern","trans":"n. 暗模式（恶意欺骗界面）"},{"word":"manipulation","trans":"n. 操纵，摆布"},{"word":"deceptive","trans":"adj. 欺骗性的"},{"word":"opt-out","trans":"v./n. 退出，不加入"},{"word":"coercive","trans":"adj. 强迫的，胁迫的"},{"word":"regulatory","trans":"adj. 监管的"}]},{"id":"eng2_2022_t4","exam":"英语二","year":"2022","text_num":"Text 4","title":"高校伦理道德课程能否真正改变人们实际行为","difficulty":"偏难★★★★","summary":"报道《认知》期刊的一项校园实证研究：尽管学界原本对伦理课能否改变实际行为存疑，但一次关于工厂化养殖肉类伦理的课堂讨论竟使学生连续数周的含肉餐消费明显下降；文中同时呈现外部学者的审慎质疑与研究者对行为成因的剖析。","paragraphs":["Although ethics classes are common around the world, scientists are unsure if their lessons can actually change behavior; evidence either way is weak, relying on contrived laboratory tests or sometimes unreliable self-reports. But a new study published in Cognition found that, in at least one real-world situation, a single ethics lesson may have had lasting effects.","The researchers investigated one class session's impact on eating meat. They chose this particular behavior for three reasons, according to study co-author Eric Schwitzgebel, a philosopher at the University of California, Riverside: students' attitudes on the topic are variable and unstable, behavior is easily measurable, and ethics literature largely agrees that eating less meat is good because it reduces environmental harm and animal suffering. Half of the students in four large philosophy classes read an article on the ethics of factory-farmed meat, optionally watched an 11-minute video on the topic and joined a 50-minute discussion. The other half focused on charitable giving instead. Then, unknown to the students, the researchers studied their anonymized meal-card purchases for that semester- nearly 14,000 receipts for almost 500 students.","Schwitzgebel predicted the intervention would have no effect; he had previously found that ethics professors do not differ from other professors on a range of behaviors, including voting rates, blood donation and returning library books. But among student subjects who discussed meat ethics, meal purchases containing meat decreased from 52 to 45 percent- and this effect held steady for the study's duration of several weeks. Purchases from the other group remained at 52 percent.","“That's actually a pretty large effect for a pretty small intervention,\" Schwitzgebel says. Psychologist Nina Strohminger at the University of Pennsylvania, who was not involved in the study, says she wants the effect to be real but cannot rule out some unknown confounding variable. And if real, she notes, it might be reversible by another nudge: \"Easy come, easy go.”","Schwitzgebel suspects the greatest impact came from social influence-classmates or teaching assistants leading the discussions may have shared their own vegetarianism, showing it as achievable or more common. Second, the video may have had an emotional impact. Least rousing, he thinks, was rational argument, although his co-authors say reason might play a bigger role. Now the researchers are probing the specific effects of teaching style, teaching assistants' eating habits and students' video exposure. Meanwhile, Schwitzgebel- who had predicted no effect- will be eating his words."],"questions":[{"q_num":36,"stem":"Scientists generally believe that the effects of ethics classes are","options":{"A":"hard to determine.","B":"narrowly interpreted.","C":"difficult to ignore.","D":"poorly summarized."},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":1,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第1段首句：科学家们并不确定伦理课能否真正改变行为（scientists are unsure if their lessons can actually change behavior），正反两方面的证据都很薄弱，说明其效果难以确定。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第1段首句明确指出：“scientists are unsure if their lessons can actually change behavior; evidence either way is weak, relying on contrived laboratory tests or sometimes unreliable self-reports.”证据薄弱、尚不确定，精准对应 hard to determine（难以确定）。","B":"【无中生有】原文批评证据薄弱、依赖人为实验室测试或不可靠的自陈报告，并未提及效果被“狭隘解读（narrowly interpreted）”。","C":"【正反混淆】原文强调科学家不确定伦理课是否有效，而非说其效果“难以忽视（difficult to ignore）”。","D":"【偷换概念】原文问题是缺乏可靠实证证据，而非“总结得不好（poorly summarized）”。"}},{"q_num":37,"stem":"Which of the following is a reason for the researchers to study meat eating?","options":{"A":"It is common among students.","B":"It is a behavior easy to measure.","C":"It is important to students' health.","D":"It is a hot topic in ethics classes."},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":2,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第2段第二句：研究者选择“吃肉”这一行为基于三大理由——学生态度多变不稳定、行为易于衡量（behavior is easily measurable）、伦理文献普遍认同少吃肉有益。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【无中生有】第2段给出的第一条理由是学生对吃肉的态度不稳定（variable and unstable），而非“吃肉在学生中很普遍”。","B":"【正解】第2段第二句直接列明三大理由之一为“behavior is easily measurable”，后文亦印证可通过匿名饭卡消费记录直接统计，精准对应 It is a behavior easy to measure。","C":"【无中生有】第2段提到少吃肉可减少环境危害和动物痛苦（reduces environmental harm and animal suffering），并未提及对学生健康的重要性。","D":"【偷换概念】原文仅说伦理文献普遍赞同少吃肉（ethics literature largely agrees），并未说这是伦理课堂的热门话题（hot topic）。"}},{"q_num":38,"stem":"Eric Schwitzgebel's previous findings suggest that ethics professors","options":{"A":"are seldom critical of their students.","B":"are less sociable than other professors.","C":"are not sensitive to political issues.","D":"are not necessarily ethically better."},"answer":"D","hint":{"para":3,"type":"细节推断题","focus":"定位第3段首句：Schwitzgebel先前发现，伦理学教授在投票率、献血和归还图书馆藏书等一系列日常行为上与其他教授并无差异（do not differ from other professors），说明他们未必在道德上更高尚。"},"question_type":"细节推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【无中生有】第3段并未提及伦理学教授是否批评学生（seldom critical of their students）。","B":"【无中生有】原文未对比伦理学教授与其他教授的社交能力（less sociable）。","C":"【偷换概念】原文仅以投票率（voting rates）作为日常公民行为的举例之一，说明两类教授无差异，而非说伦理学教授“对政治议题不敏感”。","D":"【正解】第3段首句指出Schwitzgebel先前发现伦理学教授在投票、献血、按时还书等道德相关行为上与其他教授没有差别（do not differ from other professors），表明其道德表现未必更优，精准对应 are not necessarily ethically better。"}},{"q_num":39,"stem":"Nina Strohminger thinks that the effect of the intervention is","options":{"A":"permanent.","B":"predictable.","C":"uncertain.","D":"unrepeatable."},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":4,"type":"观点态度题","focus":"定位第4段后两句：未参与研究的心理学家Nina Strohminger表示，她希望这一效果是真的，但无法排除某些未知混淆变量（cannot rule out some unknown confounding variable），且即便为真也可能轻易逆转，说明她认为干预效果尚不确定（uncertain）。"},"question_type":"观点态度题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正反混淆】第4段末句她直言即使效果为真，也可能被另一次助推轻易逆转（might be reversible by another nudge: \"Easy come, easy go.\"），与“永久（permanent）”完全相反。","B":"【正反混淆】她指出存在无法排除的未知混淆变量（unknown confounding variable），说明效果并不可预测（predictable）。","C":"【正解】第4段指出Nina Strohminger虽希望效果真实，但“cannot rule out some unknown confounding variable（不能排除未知混淆变量）”，还提出“if real... might be reversible”，对干预效果的真实性与持久性持审慎存疑态度，精准对应 uncertain（不确定的）。","D":"【偷换概念】她怀疑的是实验可能受未知混淆变量干扰且效果可逆（reversible），并未声称该干预效果“不可重复（unrepeatable）”。"}},{"q_num":40,"stem":"Eric Schwitzgebel suspects that the students' change in behavior","options":{"A":"can bring psychological benefits.","B":"can be analyzed statistically.","C":"is a result of multiple factors.","D":"is a sign of self-development."},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":5,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第5段前三句：Schwitzgebel推测最大影响来自同伴与助教的社会影响（social influence），其次是视频的情感冲击（emotional impact），作用最小的是理性论证（rational argument），可见行为改变是多重因素共同作用的结果。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【无中生有】第5段提到视频可能带来情感冲击，并未提及学生行为改变会带来“心理益处（psychological benefits）”。","B":"【无中生有】末段提到研究者正进一步探究教学风格、助教饮食习惯等因素的具体作用，并未说他怀疑行为改变“可以做统计分析”。","C":"【正解】第5段Schwitzgebel依次列出三个层面的诱因：首要为社会影响（greatest impact came from social influence）、其次为视频的情感冲击（Second, the video may have had an emotional impact）、最次为理性论证（Least rousing... rational argument），清楚表明他认为学生行为变化是多因素共同作用的结果（is a result of multiple factors）。","D":"【无中生有】第5段完全未提及这是“自我发展的标志（sign of self-development）”。"}}],"detailed_analysis":"本文探讨高校伦理课能否真正影响现实行为。以往证据薄弱，哲学家Eric Schwitzgebel本人过去的研究也曾发现伦理学教授在投票、献血等行为上并不比其他教授更道德。然而他在《认知》发表的新实验通过追踪近500名学生的饭卡消费发现，讨论肉类伦理的实验组含肉餐比例从52%降至45%并维持数周。不过，外部心理学家Nina Strohminger提醒该效果可能受未知混淆变量影响且易被逆转；Schwitzgebel则推测行为改变主要源于社会影响、情感冲击与理性论证等多重因素的共同作用。","keywords":[{"word":"ethics","trans":"n. 伦理学，道德规范"},{"word":"philosophical","trans":"adj. 哲学的"},{"word":"integrity","trans":"n. 道德操守"},{"word":"disconnect","trans":"n. 脱节，脱节现象"},{"word":"normative","trans":"adj. 规范的"},{"word":"altruism","trans":"n. 利他主义"}]},{"id":"eng2_2023_t3","exam":"英语二","year":"2023","text_num":"Text 3","title":"数字时代互联网对人类记忆模式与认知的重构","difficulty":"偏难★★★★","summary":"探讨互联网对人类记忆机制的重构：Betsy Sparrow的研究表明，大脑并未退化，而是通过“认知外包”将记忆重点从具体事实转向信息存储位置；其他学者则指出互联网对大脑的长期影响尚待更多实证研究。","paragraphs":["The Internet may be changing merely what we remember, not our capacity to do so, suggests Columbia University psychology professor Betsy Sparrow. In 2011, Sparrow led a study in which participants were asked to record 40 factoids in a computer (\"an ostrich's eye is bigger than its brain,\" for example). Half of the participants were told the information would be erased, while the other half were told it would be saved. Guess what? The latter group made no effort to recall the information when quizzed on it later, because they knew they could find it on their computers. In the same study, a group was asked to remember both the information and the folders it was stored in. They didn't remember the information, but they remembered how to find the folders. In other words, human memory is not deteriorating but \"adapting to new communications technology,\" Sparrow says.","In a very practical way, the Internet is becoming an external hard drive for our memories, a process known as \"cognitive offloading.\" Traditionally, this role was fulfilled by data banks, libraries, and other humans. Your father may never remember birthdays because your mother does, for instance. Some worry that this is having a destructive effect on society, but Sparrow sees an upside. Perhaps, she suggests, the trend will change our approach to learning from a focus on individual facts and memorization to an emphasis on more conceptual thinking- something that is not available on the Internet. \"I personally have never seen all that much intellectual value in memorizing things,\" Sparrow says, adding that we haven't lost our ability to do it.","Still other experts say it's too soon to understand how the Internet affects our brains. There is no experimental evidence showing that it interferes with our ability to focus, for instance, wrote psychologists Christopher Chabris and Daniel J. Simons. And surfing the web exercised the brain more than reading did among computer-savvy older adults in a 2008 study involving 24 participants at the Semel Institute for Neuroscience and Human Behavior at the University of California, Los Angeles.","\"There may be costs associated with our increased reliance on the Internet, but I'd have to imagine that overall the benefits are going to outweigh those costs,\" observes psychology professor Benjamin Storm. \"It seems pretty clear that memory is changing, but is it changing for the better? At this point, we don't know.”"],"questions":[{"q_num":31,"stem":"Sparrow's study shows that with the Internet, the human brain will ____.","options":{"A":"analyze information in detail","B":"collect information efficiently","C":"switch its focus of memory","D":"extend its memory duration"},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":1,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第1段：首句指出互联网改变的只是“我们记什么（what we remember）”而非记忆能力；实验显示受试者没记住具体信息，却记住了如何找到文件夹（remembered how to find the folders），即转移了记忆重心。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正反混淆】第1段实验表明得知信息会被保存的受试者根本不费力回忆具体事实，并未说大脑会“详细分析信息”。","B":"【偷换概念】实验考查的是人们在电脑辅助下的记忆方式（记位置而非记内容），并非强调“高效收集信息（collect information efficiently）”。","C":"【正解】第1段首句即指出互联网改变的是“what we remember”，实验进一步发现受试者记不住具体信息，却牢记如何找到存放文件夹（remembered how to find the folders），精准对应 switch its focus of memory（转移记忆重心）。","D":"【无中生有】第1段并未提及互联网会“延长记忆持续时间（extend its memory duration）”。"}},{"q_num":32,"stem":"The process of \"cognitive offloading\" ____.","options":{"A":"helps us identify false information","B":"keeps our memory from failing","C":"enables us to classify trivial facts","D":"lessens our memory burdens"},"answer":"D","hint":{"para":2,"type":"细节/词义理解题","focus":"定位第2段前两句：互联网正成为我们记忆的外置硬盘（an external hard drive for our memories），这一过程被称为“认知外包（cognitive offloading）”，就像母亲替父亲记生日一样，把记忆任务分担出去，减轻了大脑的记忆负担。"},"question_type":"细节/词义理解题","option_analysis":{"A":"【无中生有】第2段完全未提及认知外包有助于识别虚假信息（identify false information）。","B":"【偷换概念】第1段说人类记忆本身并未衰退而是在适应，并非靠认知外包来“防止记忆失效（keeps our memory from failing）”。","C":"【无中生有】原文未提及认知外包能帮我们对琐碎事实分类（classify trivial facts）。","D":"【正解】第2段首句将互联网比作人类记忆的“外置硬盘（external hard drive）”，随后举例“父亲因母亲记得生日而自己不必去记”，生动说明“cognitive offloading（认知卸载/外包）”把记忆任务交由外部承担，减轻了我们的记忆负担（lessens our memory burdens）。"}},{"q_num":33,"stem":"Which of the following would Sparrow support about the Internet?","options":{"A":"It may reform our learning approach.","B":"It may impact our society negatively.","C":"It may enhance our adaptability to technology.","D":"It may interfere with our conceptual thinking."},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":2,"type":"观点态度题","focus":"定位第2段第五句：Sparrow看到了积极一面，认为这一趋势或许会改变我们的学习方式——从关注零散事实和死记硬背转向更加重视概念性思维（change our approach to learning from... to...）。"},"question_type":"观点态度题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第2段Sparrow明确提出：“Perhaps, she suggests, the trend will change our approach to learning from a focus on individual facts and memorization to an emphasis on more conceptual thinking”，其中“change our approach to learning”精准对应 reform our learning approach（改革我们的学习方式）。","B":"【张冠李戴】担忧该趋势对社会有破坏性影响（destructive effect on society）的是“Some（一些人）”，Sparrow本人恰恰看到了积极面（sees an upside）。","C":"【偷换概念】第1段说的是人类记忆正在适应新技术，而非Sparrow主张互联网会“增强我们对技术的适应能力”。","D":"【正反混淆】Sparrow认为互联网促使学习转向更重视概念性思维（an emphasis on more conceptual thinking），是促进而非干扰（interfere with）概念性思维。"}},{"q_num":34,"stem":"It is indicated in Paragraph 3 that how the Internet affects our brains ____.","options":{"A":"requires further academic research","B":"is most studied in older adults","C":"is reflected in our reading speed","D":"depends on our web-surfing habits"},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":3,"type":"细节推断题","focus":"定位第3段前两句：其他专家表示，现在要弄清互联网如何影响大脑还为时过早（it's too soon to understand how the Internet affects our brains），且目前缺乏实验证据，可见仍需进一步学术研究。"},"question_type":"细节推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第3段首两句明确指出：“Still other experts say it's too soon to understand how the Internet affects our brains. There is no experimental evidence showing that...”，表明目前尚无定论、缺乏实验证据，需要进一步学术研究（requires further academic research）。","B":"【以偏概全】第3段末句仅提及2008年一项涉及24名熟悉电脑的老年人的研究，并未说明该课题“主要在老年人中开展研究（most studied in older adults）”。","C":"【偷换概念】2008年研究对比的是上网与阅读对大脑的锻炼程度（exercised the brain more than reading did），未提及阅读速度（reading speed）。","D":"【无中生有】第3段并未提及互联网对大脑的影响取决于“上网习惯（web-surfing habits）”。"}},{"q_num":35,"stem":"Neither Sparrow nor Storm would agree that ____.","options":{"A":"our reliance on the Internet will be costly","B":"the Internet is weakening our memory","C":"memory exercise is a must for our brains","D":"our ability to focus declines with age"},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":4,"type":"观点比较题","focus":"定位第1、2段与第4段：Sparrow明确表示人类记忆并未退化（not deteriorating）且未丧失记忆能力（haven't lost our ability to do it）；Storm认为利大于弊，且尚不清楚记忆变化是好是坏（At this point, we don't know）。因此两人都不赞同“互联网正在削弱我们的记忆”。"},"question_type":"观点比较题","option_analysis":{"A":"【张冠李戴】第4段首句Storm明确承认“There may be costs associated with our increased reliance on the Internet”，既然Storm认可存在代价，便不符合题干“两人均不同意（Neither... would agree）”。","B":"【正解】第1段Sparrow强调记忆并非退化而是在适应（not deteriorating but adapting），第2段又称我们并未丧失记忆能力；第4段Storm则指出总体益处可能大于代价，且目前无法断定记忆变化是好是坏。因此两人均不会同意“互联网正在削弱我们的记忆（the Internet is weakening our memory）”。","C":"【无中生有】两人均未讨论“记忆锻炼对大脑是否必需”，该项并非两人共同否定的观点。","D":"【无中生有】第3段提及其他学者关于专注力和老年人的研究，但Sparrow和Storm均未探讨“专注力是否随年龄下降”。"}}],"detailed_analysis":"本文客观分析互联网如何改变人类记忆。哥伦比亚大学心理学家Betsy Sparrow的2011年实验发现，得知信息会被电脑保存的受试者不再费力记内容，而是记住查找文件夹的路径，说明记忆是在适应新技术而非退化。她认为这种“认知外包”有望推动学习从死记硬背转向概念性思维。后两段引入Chabris、Simons及Storm等学者观点，指出目前尚无证据证明上网损害专注力，但记忆改变究竟利弊几何仍需进一步研究。","keywords":[{"word":"transactive memory","trans":"n. 交互式记忆，分布式记忆"},{"word":"cognitive","trans":"adj. 认知的"},{"word":"retrieval","trans":"n. 检索，恢复"},{"word":"offload","trans":"v. 卸载，外包"},{"word":"interconnected","trans":"adj. 互联互通的"},{"word":"externalize","trans":"v. 使外部化"}]},{"id":"eng2_2024_t3","exam":"英语二","year":"2024","text_num":"Text 3","title":"高龄驾驶员的安全隐患与适驾能力评估挑战","difficulty":"偏难★★★★","summary":"探讨如何让不再适合驾车的高龄驾驶员安全离开道路的现实难题，分析各州对医生上报规定不一、跨领域治理碎片化以及老年人视力与记忆障碍等痛点，并指出开发适老汽车才是长远之策。","paragraphs":["One of the biggest challenges in keeping unsafe aging drivers off the road is convincing them that it's time to turn over the keys. \"It's a complete life-changer” when someone stops- or is forced to stop- driving, said former risk manager Anne M. Menke.","“The American Medical Association advises physicians that 'in situations where clear evidence of substantial driving impairment implies a strong threat to patient and public safety, and where the physician's advice to discontinue driving privileges is ignored, it is desirable and ethical to notify the Department of Motor Vehicles,'\" Menke wrote. \"Some states require physicians to report, others allow but do not mandate reports, while a few consider a report a breach of confidentiality. There could be liability and penalties if a physician does not act in accordance with state laws on reporting and confidentiality,\" she counseled.","Part of the problem in keeping older drivers safe is that the difficulties are addressed piecemeal by different professions with different focuses, including gerontologists, highway administration officials, automotive engineers and others, said gerontologist Elizabeth Dugan. \"There's not a National Institute of Older Driver Studies,\" she said. \"We need better evidence on what makes drivers unsafe\" and what can help, said Dugan.","One thing that does seem to work is requiring drivers to report in person for license renewal. Mandatory in-person renewal was associated with a 31 per cent reduction in fatal crashes involving drivers 85 or older, according to one study. Passing vision tests also produced a similar decline in fatal crashes for those drivers, although there appeared to be no benefit from combining the two.","Many older drivers don't see eye doctors or can't afford to. Primary care providers have their hands full and may not be able to follow through with patients who have trouble driving because they can't turn their heads or remember where they are going—or have gotten shorter and haven't changed their seat settings sufficiently to reach car pedals easily.","As long as there are other cars on the roads, self-driving cars won't solve the problems of crashes, said Dugan. Avoiding dangers posed by all those human drivers would require too many algorithms, she said. But we need to do more to improve safety, said Dugan. \"If we're going to have 100-year lives, we need cars that a 90-year-old can drive comfortably.\""],"questions":[{"q_num":31,"stem":"According to Paragraph 1, keeping unsafe aging drivers off the road ____.","options":{"A":"is a new safety measure","B":"has become a disputed issue","C":"can be a tough task to complete","D":"will be beneficial to their health"},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":1,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第1段首句：让不安全的高龄司机不再上路面临的最大挑战之一（One of the biggest challenges），就是说服他们该交出车钥匙了，因为停驾会彻底改变生活，说明这是一项棘手的任务。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【无中生有】第1段并未称让不安全的高龄司机停驾是一项“新的安全措施（new safety measure）”。","B":"【无中生有】第1段强调的是劝说停驾很难做到，而非说这件事本身引发争议（disputed issue）。","C":"【正解】第1段首句直接指出“One of the biggest challenges in keeping unsafe aging drivers off the road is convincing them that it's time to turn over the keys”，且停驾是“a complete life-changer”，精准对应 can be a tough task to complete（可能是一项难以完成的任务）。","D":"【无中生有】第1段未提及停止驾车会对老年人的健康有益（beneficial to their health）。"}},{"q_num":32,"stem":"The American Medical Association's advice ____.","options":{"A":"has won support from drivers","B":"is generally considered unrealistic","C":"is widely dismissed as unnecessary","D":"has met with different responses"},"answer":"D","hint":{"para":2,"type":"细节推断题","focus":"定位第2段第二句：对于美国医学会建议医生上报严重驾驶障碍患者的做法，有些州强制要求上报，有些州允许但不强制，还有少数州甚至视之为违反保密义务——可见各州反应各异。"},"question_type":"细节推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【无中生有】第2段讲的是各州法律对医生上报的不同规定，并未提及该建议获得了司机支持。","B":"【无中生有】原文并未提到该建议被普遍认为不切实际（unrealistic）。","C":"【无中生有】原文并未称该建议被广泛当作不必要而驳回（widely dismissed as unnecessary）。","D":"【正解】第2段明确列出各州截然不同的法律态度：“Some states require physicians to report, others allow but do not mandate reports, while a few consider a report a breach of confidentiality”，精准概括为 has met with different responses（遭遇了不同反应）。"}},{"q_num":33,"stem":"According to Dugan, efforts to keep older drivers safe ____.","options":{"A":"have brought about big changes","B":"need to be well coordinated","C":"have gained public recognition","D":"call for relevant legal support"},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":3,"type":"细节推断题","focus":"定位第3段：Dugan指出保护高龄司机安全的部分症结在于问题被不同侧重点的行业零散处理（addressed piecemeal by different professions），且缺乏国家级的专门研究机构，可见相关努力需要统筹协调。"},"question_type":"细节推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正反混淆】Dugan批评当前举措支离破碎（piecemeal）、缺乏充分证据，并未说已带来巨大变革（big changes）。","B":"【正解】第3段Dugan明确指出难题由老年学家、公路管理官员、汽车工程师等不同专业各自为政地零散处理（addressed piecemeal by different professions with different focuses），缺乏统一的“国家高龄驾驶者研究所”，反推出各方努力亟需良好协调（need to be well coordinated）。","C":"【无中生有】第3段并未提及这些努力已获得公众认可（public recognition）。","D":"【张冠李戴】各州法律规定是第2段Menke讨论的内容，第3段Dugan呼吁的是统筹研究与更好证据，并未呼吁法律支持。"}},{"q_num":34,"stem":"Some older drivers have trouble driving because they tend to ____.","options":{"A":"stick with bad driving habits","B":"have a weakened memory","C":"suffer from chronic pains","D":"neglect car maintenance"},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":5,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第5段第二句：部分高龄患者驾车困难是因为无法顺利转头、记不清自己要去哪儿（remember where they are going），或身高变矮却未调好座椅以够到踏板。其中“记不清要去哪儿”即记忆力减退。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【无中生有】第5段列举的是身体与认知退化原因，并未提及固守不良驾驶习惯（bad driving habits）。","B":"【正解】第5段第二句明确列出高龄患者驾车困难的原因之一是“can't... remember where they are going（记不住自己要去哪里）”，精准同义替换为 have a weakened memory（记忆力减弱）。","C":"【无中生有】原文提及无法转头、记忆减退和身高变矮，并未提及遭受慢性疼痛（chronic pains）。","D":"【偷换概念】原文说老人未充分调整座椅位置（haven't changed their seat settings），并非“忽视车辆保养（neglect car maintenance）”。"}},{"q_num":35,"stem":"Dugan thinks that the solution to the problems of crashes may lie in ____.","options":{"A":"upgrading self-driving vehicles","B":"developing senior-friendly cars","C":"renovating transport facilities","D":"adjusting the age limit for drivers"},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":6,"type":"观点态度题","focus":"定位第6段：Dugan先否定自动驾驶汽车能解决车祸问题，继而提出建设性方向——如果人类将活到100岁，我们需要90岁老人也能舒适驾驶的汽车（cars that a 90-year-old can drive comfortably），即研发适老汽车。"},"question_type":"观点态度题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正反混淆】第6段首句Dugan明确否定自动驾驶方案：“As long as there are other cars on the roads, self-driving cars won't solve the problems of crashes.”","B":"【正解】第6段末句Dugan直言：“If we're going to have 100-year lives, we need cars that a 90-year-old can drive comfortably.”能供90岁长者舒适驾驶的汽车精准对应 developing senior-friendly cars（开发适老友好型汽车）。","C":"【无中生有】第6段聚焦汽车本身的设计适配，并未提及改造交通设施（renovating transport facilities）。","D":"【无中生有】第6段并未提议调整驾驶员年龄上限（adjusting the age limit）。"}}],"detailed_analysis":"本文聚焦高龄驾驶安全议题。开篇即指出说服高龄司机交出车钥匙是极大挑战，因为停驾彻底改变其生活。接着剖析美国医学会关于医生上报的建议在各州遭遇截然不同的法律回应，并借老年学家Elizabeth Dugan之口批评当前各专业各自为政、缺乏统一协调。文中肯定了现场亲自换证和视力测试对降低致命车祸的效果，同时指出基层医疗难以跟进老人记忆减退、转头困难等问题；末段Dugan认为自动驾驶无法解决混合交通车祸，真正出路在于研发让90岁老人也能舒适驾驶的适老汽车。","keywords":[{"word":"aging drivers","trans":"n. 高龄驾驶员"},{"word":"mobility","trans":"n. 行动能力，流动性"},{"word":"cognitive decline","trans":"n. 认知能力衰退"},{"word":"autonomy","trans":"n. 自主权，独立性"},{"word":"assessment","trans":"n. 评估，测评"},{"word":"intervention","trans":"n. 干预措施"}]},{"id":"eng2_2025_t2","exam":"英语二","year":"2025","text_num":"Text 2","title":"与其修补NHS，不如从根本上反思健康之道","difficulty":"困难★★★★★","summary":"剖析英国国民医疗服务体系（NHS）创立近75年后面临的模式过时、排队冗长与人手紧绷等危机，介绍Reform智库发起的“重新构想健康”计划，主张从单纯“修补医院医疗”转向基层预防、重视健康社会决定因素并向地方下放权责。","paragraphs":["When it was established, the National Health Service (NHS) was visionary: offering high-quality, timely care to meet the dominant needs of the population it served. Nearly 75 years on, with the UK facing very different health challenges, it is clear that the model is out of date.","From life expectancy to cancer and infant mortality rates, we are lagging behind many of our peers. With more than 6.8 million on waitlists, healthcare is becoming increasingly inaccessible for those who cannot opt to pay for private treatment; and the cost of providing healthcare is increasingly squeezing out investment in other public services. As demand for healthcare continues to grow, pressures on the workforce—which is already near breaking point— will only become more acute.","Many of the answers to the crisis in health and care are well rehearsed. We need to be much better at reducing and diverting demand on health services, rather than simply managing it. Much more needs to be invested in communities and primary care to reduce our reliance on hospitals. And capacity in social care needs to be greater, to support the growing number of people living with long-term conditions.","Yet despite two decades of strategies and a number of major health reforms, we have failed to make meaningful progress on any of these aims. That is why the Reform think tank is launching a new programme of work entitled “Reimagining health”, supported by ten former health ministers. Together, we are calling for a much more open and honest conversation about the future of health in the UK, and an “urgent rethink” of the hospital-centric model we retain.","This must begin with the question of how we maximise the health of the nation, rather than “fix” the NHS. It is estimated, for example, that healthcare accounts for only about 20% of health outcomes. Much more important are the places we live, work and socialise—yet there is no clear cross-government strategy for improving these social determinants of health. Worse, when policies like the national obesity strategy are scrapped, taxpayers are left with the heavy price tag of treating the illnesses, like diabetes, that result.","Reform wants to ask how power and resources should be distributed in our health system. What health functions should remain at the centre, and what should be given to local leaders, often responsible for services that create health, and with a much better understanding of the needs of their populations?"],"questions":[{"q_num":26,"stem":"According to the first two paragraphs, the NHS ____.","options":{"A":"is troubled by funding deficiencies","B":"can hardly satisfy people’s needs","C":"can barely retain its current employees","D":"is rivalled by private medical services"},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":2,"type":"细节概括题","focus":"定位第1–2段：第1段指出创立时曾满足民众主导需求的NHS如今模式已过时；第2段列举英国多项健康指标落后、超680万人排队、医疗越来越难以获得，可见NHS已难以满足民众需求。"},"question_type":"细节概括题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偷换概念】第2段说医疗成本正挤压对其他公共服务的投资（squeezing out investment in other public services），强调的是耗资巨大而非NHS自身“受资金短缺困扰”。","B":"【正解】第1段对比称NHS创立之初能满足民众主导需求，而近75年后模式已过时（out of date）；第2段接着指出英国在预期寿命等指标上落后同行，超680万人排队，对无力自费者而言医疗愈发难以获得（increasingly inaccessible），综合表明NHS难以满足民众需求（can hardly satisfy people's needs）。","C":"【偷换概念】第2段末句仅说医护人员面临的压力接近崩溃边缘（near breaking point）且将愈发严峻，并未说“几乎留不住现有员工（can barely retain its current employees）”。","D":"【无中生有】第2段仅顺带提及无力支付私立医疗的人群看病难，并未讨论私立医疗对NHS构成竞争威胁（rivalled by private medical services）。"}},{"q_num":27,"stem":"One answer to the crisis in health and care is to ____.","options":{"A":"boost the efficiency of hospitals","B":"lighten the burden on social care","C":"increase resources for primary care","D":"reduce the pressure on communities"},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":3,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第3段第三句：应对危机的一个明确对策是向社区和初级/基层医疗投入更多资源（Much more needs to be invested in communities and primary care），以减少对医院的依赖。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正反混淆】第3段主张减少对医院的依赖（reduce our reliance on hospitals），而非提高医院效率（boost the efficiency of hospitals）。","B":"【偷换概念】第3段末句说的是“扩大社会照护能力（capacity in social care needs to be greater）”以支持长期病患，而非“减轻社会照护的负担”。","C":"【正解】第3段明确提出：“Much more needs to be invested in communities and primary care to reduce our reliance on hospitals.”“invest much more in... primary care”精准同义替换为 increase resources for primary care（增加基层医疗资源）。","D":"【偷换概念】原文主张加大对社区的投入以分流医院压力，并非“减轻社区的压力（reduce the pressure on communities）”。"}},{"q_num":28,"stem":"\"Reimagining health\" is aimed to ____.","options":{"A":"reinforce hospital management","B":"readjust healthcare regulations","C":"restructure the health system","D":"resume suspended health reforms"},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":4,"type":"细节推断题","focus":"定位第4段（结合第5–6段）：鉴于过去二十年改革收效甚微，Reform智库发起“重新构想健康”计划，呼吁对英国健康未来展开坦诚对话，并对现有以医院为中心的模式进行“紧急反思（urgent rethink）”，即重构整个健康体系。"},"question_type":"细节推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正反混淆】该计划质疑并反思“以医院为中心的模式（hospital-centric model）”，并非强化医院管理（reinforce hospital management）。","B":"【偷换概念】计划呼吁的是对医疗健康模式、目标与权力分配的根本重塑，而非单纯微调医疗监管规章（readjust healthcare regulations）。","C":"【正解】第4段指出“Reimagining health”旨在对英国健康未来展开开放讨论并“紧急反思”现有的医院中心模式，第5–6段进一步说明其立足点在于超越“修补NHS”、重新分配健康体系的权力和资源，精准对应 restructure the health system（重构健康体系）。","D":"【无中生有】第4段说过去二十年的多项战略和改革未能取得实质进展，并非该计划旨在“重启被搁置的医疗改革（resume suspended health reforms）”。"}},{"q_num":29,"stem":"To maximise the nation's health, the author suggests ____.","options":{"A":"introducing relevant taxation policies","B":"paying due attention to social factors","C":"reevaluating major health outcomes","D":"enhancing the quality of health care"},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":5,"type":"细节推断题","focus":"定位第5段：医疗仅占健康结果的约20%，更重要的是我们居住、工作和社交的环境（社会决定因素），但目前缺乏改善这些健康社会决定因素的跨部门战略，可见作者主张重视社会因素。"},"question_type":"细节推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【望文生义】第5段末句提到取消国家肥胖战略让纳税人（taxpayers）承担高昂治病代价，并未建议出台新的税收政策（taxation policies）。","B":"【正解】第5段明确指出医疗仅贡献约20%的健康结果，“Much more important are the places we live, work and socialise”，并批评缺乏改善这些“social determinants of health（健康社会决定因素）”的跨政府战略，精准对应 paying due attention to social factors（给予社会因素应有重视）。","C":"【偷换概念】作者引用20%的比例是为了突出社会环境因素比医疗本身更关键，并非建议“重新评估主要健康结果指标”。","D":"【正反混淆】第5段开篇即强调要思考如何最大化国民健康而非仅仅“修复”NHS，并指出医疗本身只占健康结果的20%，故“提升医疗质量”并非本段核心建议。"}},{"q_num":30,"stem":"It can be inferred that local leaders should ____.","options":{"A":"exercise their power more reasonably","B":"develop a stronger sense of responsibility","C":"play a bigger role in the health system","D":"understand people’s health needs better"},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":6,"type":"推断题","focus":"定位第6段：末段追问哪些健康职能应留给中央、哪些应交给地方领导者——并顺势肯定地方领导者本就负责创造健康的服务且更了解当地民众需求，言下之意是应下放权责，让地方领导者在健康体系中发挥更大作用。"},"question_type":"推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偷换概念】第6段讨论的是中央与地方之间如何重新分配权力与资源（how power and resources should be distributed），而非批评地方领导者行使现有权力不够合理。","B":"【偷换概念】原文指出地方领导者“通常负责创造健康的服务（often responsible for services that create health）”，强调的是其既定角色优势，而非要求他们“增强责任感”。","C":"【正解】第6段探讨健康体系内权力与资源分配，设问哪些职能应交给地方领导者，并肯定其负责创造健康的服务且更了解本地民众需求，显然暗示应向地方下放更多职能与资源，让地方领导者在健康体系中发挥更大作用（play a bigger role in the health system）。","D":"【偷换概念】原文肯定地方领导者“已经对当地人口需求有更好的了解（with a much better understanding of the needs of their populations）”，这是赋权给他们的理由，而非要求他们“进一步去更好理解需求”。"}}],"detailed_analysis":"本文探讨英国NHS的系统性困境与根本出路。文章指出，拥有近75年历史的NHS模式已经过时，超680万人候诊、公共医疗日益难以获得且挤压其他公共服务投入。作者强调必须增加社区和基层医疗投资、扩大社会照护能力，并介绍由十位前卫生大臣支持的“重新构想健康（Reimagining health）”计划，呼吁彻底反思以医院为中心的旧模式，正视占健康结果约80%的社会环境因素，同时赋予更了解本地需求的地方领导者更大职能。","keywords":[{"word":"reimagine","trans":"v. 重新构想，根本反思"},{"word":"deficiency","trans":"n. 缺陷，不足"},{"word":"preventative","trans":"adj. 预防性的"},{"word":"infrastructure","trans":"n. 基础设施"},{"word":"holistic","trans":"adj. 全面的，整体的"},{"word":"wellbeing","trans":"n. 健康福祉"}]},{"id":"eng2_2025_t3","exam":"英语二","year":"2025","text_num":"Text 3","title":"印度极端高温行动计划(HAPs)的实施挑战","difficulty":"困难★★★★★","summary":"介绍印度各地迅速推广的高温行动计划（HAPs），剖析现有计划在资金、本地化预警标准及忽视湿度因素等方面的不足，并引用城市规划师Kotharkar等学者建议：绘制脆弱性地图、将短期应急拓展为中长期降温与城市改造。","paragraphs":["Heat action plans, or HAPs, have been proliferating in India in the past few years. In general, an HAP spells out when and how officials should issue heat warnings and alert hospitals and other institutions. Nagpur’s plan, for instance, calls for hospitals to set aside “cold wards” in the summer for treating heatstroke patients, and advises builders to give construction laborers a break from work on very hot days.","But implementation of existing HAPs has been uneven, according to a report from the Center for Policy Research. Many lack adequate funding, it found. And their triggering thresholds often are not customized to the local climate. In some areas, high daytime temperatures alone might serve as an adequate trigger for alerts. But in other places, nighttime temperatures or humidity might be as important a gauge of risk as daytime highs.","Mumbai’s April heat stroke deaths highlighted the need for more nuanced and localized warnings, researchers say. That day’s high temperature of roughly 36°C was 1°C shy of the heat wave alert threshold for coastal cities set by national meteorological authorities. But the effects of the heat were amplified by humidity—an often neglected factor in heat alert systems—and the lack of shade at the late-morning outdoor ceremony.","To help improve HAPs, urban planner Kotharkar’s team is working on a model plan that outlines best practices and could be adapted to local conditions. Among other things, she says, all cities should create a vulnerability map to help focus responses on the populations most at risk.","Such mapping doesn’t need to be complex, Kotharkar says. “A useful map can be created by looking at even a few key parameters.” For example, neighborhoods with a large elderly population or informal dwellings that cope poorly with heat could get special warnings or be bolstered with cooling centers. The Nagpur project has already created a risk and vulnerability map, which enabled Kotharkar to tell officials which neighborhoods to focus on in the event of a heat wave this summer.","HAPs shouldn’t just include short-term emergency responses, researchers say, but also recommend medium- to long-term measures that could make communities cooler. In Nagpur, for example, Kotharkar’s team has been able to advise city officials about where to plant trees to provide shade. HAPs could also guide efforts to retrofit homes or modify building regulations. “Reducing deaths in an emergency is good target to have, but it’s the lowest target,” says climate researcher Chandni Singh."],"questions":[{"q_num":31,"stem":"According to Paragraph 1, Nagpur's plan proposes measures to ____.","options":{"A":"tackle extreme weather","B":"ensure construction quality","C":"monitor emergency warnings","D":"address excessive workloads"},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":1,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第1段末句：那格浦尔的高温行动计划要求医院在夏季预留“降温病房（cold wards）”救治中暑病人，并建议建筑商在酷热天气让建筑工人暂停工作休息，均旨在应对极端高温天气。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第1段以那格浦尔市的高温行动计划为例，指出其要求医院设立夏季“降温病房”救治中暑患者，并建议建筑商在极热天气让工人休息，这些举措正是为了应对极端高温天气（tackle extreme weather）。","B":"【偷换概念】计划建议建筑商在酷热日给建筑工人放假休息，保护的是工人健康而非“确保建筑质量（ensure construction quality）”。","C":"【偷换概念】第1段称HAPs规定官员何时以及如何“发布（issue）”高温预警，而非“监测紧急预警（monitor emergency warnings）”。","D":"【偷换概念】让工人在酷热天气暂停工作是为了防范高温中暑，并非解决“工作量过大（excessive workloads）”。"}},{"q_num":32,"stem":"One problem with existing HAPs is that they ____.","options":{"A":"prove too costly to be implemented","B":"lack localized alert-issuing criteria","C":"give delayed responses to heat waves","D":"keep hospitals under great pressure"},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":2,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第2段第三句：政策研究中心报告指出，现有HAPs存在两大问题——缺乏充足资金，以及触发预警的阈值往往未按当地气候因地制宜（triggering thresholds often are not customized to the local climate）。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偷换概念】第2段指出许多计划“缺乏充足资金（lack adequate funding）”，是指经费投入不足，而非“实施成本过高以致无法推行（too costly to be implemented）”。","B":"【正解】第2段明确指出：“And their triggering thresholds often are not customized to the local climate.”触发预警的阈值未按当地气候定制，精准同义替换为 lack localized alert-issuing criteria（缺乏本地化的预警发布标准）。","C":"【无中生有】第2段批评的是实施不均、资金匮乏与阈值一刀切，并未提及对热浪“响应迟缓（delayed responses）”。","D":"【无中生有】第2段并未提及现有计划让医院承受巨大压力（keep hospitals under great pressure）。"}},{"q_num":33,"stem":"Mumbai's case shows that India's heat alert systems need to ____.","options":{"A":"include other factors besides temperature","B":"take subtle weather changes into account","C":"prioritize potentially disastrous heat waves","D":"draw further support from local authorities"},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":3,"type":"例证/细节题","focus":"定位第3段：孟买当天最高温约36°C，比国家热浪预警阈值低1°C，但高温危害被预警系统常忽略的“湿度（humidity—an often neglected factor）”以及缺乏遮阴所放大，说明预警系统不能只看温度。"},"question_type":"例证/细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第3段指出孟买致死事件当天最高温仅36°C（未达37°C预警线），但热害被“湿度——高温预警系统中常被忽视的因素（humidity—an often neglected factor in heat alert systems）”放大，说明印度高温预警系统需要把温度之外的其他因素纳入考量（include other factors besides temperature）。","B":"【偷换概念】第3段强调的是湿度等关键叠加风险因子，而非泛泛的“微妙天气变化（subtle weather changes）”。","C":"【答非所问】孟买案例剖析的是预警指标单一漏报风险，而非要求“优先应对潜在灾难性热浪”。","D":"【无中生有】第3段并未提及需要从地方当局争取更多支持（support from local authorities）。"}},{"q_num":34,"stem":"Kotharkar holds that a vulnerability map can help ____.","options":{"A":"prevent the harm of high humidity","B":"target areas needing special attention","C":"expand the Nagpur project’s coverage","D":"make relief plans for heat-stricken people"},"answer":"B","hint":{"para":4,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第4段末句与第5段：Kotharkar主张绘制脆弱性地图以将应对资源聚焦于风险最高人群（focus responses on the populations most at risk），第5段进一步举例该地图能告诉官员热浪来袭时应重点关注哪些社区（which neighborhoods to focus on）。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【张冠李戴】高湿度危害是第3段孟买案例讨论的预警因素，第4–5段脆弱性地图的作用是识别高危社区与人群，而非直接防止高湿度危害。","B":"【正解】第4段末句指出脆弱性地图有助于将应对措施集中到最脆弱人群身上（focus responses on the populations most at risk），第5段更明言那格浦尔项目的地图使Kotharkar能明确告知官员重点关注哪些社区（tell officials which neighborhoods to focus on），精准对应 target areas needing special attention（锁定需要特别关注的区域）。","C":"【无中生有】第5段仅以那格浦尔已制图为例说明地图实用有效，并未说地图用于“扩大那格浦尔项目的覆盖范围”。","D":"【偷换概念】地图用于事前锁定老龄社区、非正规住房等高危区域并发放特别预警或设降温中心，并非“为中暑受灾者制定救济方案（relief plans for heat-stricken people）”。"}},{"q_num":35,"stem":"According to the last paragraph, researchers suggest that HAPs should ____.","options":{"A":"focus more on the heatstroke treatment","B":"invite wider public participation","C":"apply for more government grants","D":"serve a broader range of purposes"},"answer":"D","hint":{"para":6,"type":"细节概括题","focus":"定位第6段：研究者指出HAPs不应局限于短期应急响应，还应涵盖使社区降温的中长期举措——如指导植树遮阴、房屋隔热改造、修订建筑规范，即发挥更广泛的综合功能。"},"question_type":"细节概括题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正反混淆】末段末句明确指出“在紧急情况下减少死亡是个好目标，但只是最低目标（it's the lowest target）”，研究者主张超越短期应急救治，而非更聚焦中暑治疗。","B":"【无中生有】第6段并未提及邀请更广泛的公众参与（wider public participation）。","C":"【无中生有】第6段未提及申请更多政府拨款（government grants）。","D":"【正解】第6段首句指出HAPs不应仅包含短期应急响应，还应推荐使社区降温的中长期举措（medium- to long-term measures），包括植树遮阴、改造住宅与修订建筑法规，精准概括为 serve a broader range of purposes（服务于更广泛的目的）。"}}],"detailed_analysis":"本文聚焦印度应对致命热浪的高温行动计划（HAPs）。开篇以那格浦尔市要求医院设“降温病房”、建议工地高温停工休息为例说明HAPs的应急作用；随后指出许多现有计划存在资金不足、预警阈值未因地制宜等问题，并以孟买4月因忽视湿度而酿成中暑死亡的案例为证。后三段介绍Kotharkar团队倡导绘制简明实用的脆弱性地图以精准定位高风险社区，并强调HAPs不应止步于紧急救治，更应纳入植树遮阴、住宅隔热改造与建筑规范修订等中长期措施。","keywords":[{"word":"heatwave","trans":"n. 热浪，极端高温"},{"word":"vulnerability","trans":"n. 脆弱性，易受害程度"},{"word":"mitigation","trans":"n. 缓解，减轻"},{"word":"informal workers","trans":"n. 非正规就业工人，户外散工"},{"word":"urban heat island","trans":"n. 热岛效应"},{"word":"resilience","trans":"n. 韧性，复原力"}]},{"id":"eng2_2025_t4","exam":"英语二","year":"2025","text_num":"Text 4","title":"城市规划中“欲望路径”（Desire Paths）揭示的人性","difficulty":"困难★★★★★","summary":"围绕城市空间中由行人自发踩踏形成的“欲望路径（Desire Paths）”展开，探讨人们追求便捷高效的本能、规划师接纳与抵制的理念冲突、历史小径演变为纽约百老汇的典故，以及人与动物共有的路径适应性。","paragraphs":["Navigating beyond the organised pavements and parks of our urban spaces, desire paths are the unofficial footprints of a community, revealing the unspoken preferences, shared shortcuts and collective choices of humans. Often appearing as trodden dirt tracks through otherwise neat green spaces, these routes of collective disobedience cut corners, bisect lawns and cross hills, representing the natural capability of people (and animals) to go from point A to point B most effectively.","Urban planners interpret desire paths as more than just convenient shortcuts; they offer valuable insights into the dynamics between planning and behaviour. Ohio State University allowed its students to navigate the Oval, a lawn in the centre of campus, freely, then proceeded to pave the desire paths, creating a web of effective routes students had established.","Yet, reluctance persists among other planners to integrate desire paths into formal plans, citing concerns about safety, environmental impact, or primarily, aesthetics. A Reddit webpage devoted to the phenomenon, boasting nearly 50,000 members, showcases images of local desire paths adorned with signs instructing pedestrians to adhere to designated walkways, underscoring the rebellious nature inherent in these human-made tracks. This clash highlights an ongoing struggle between the organic, user-driven evolution of public spaces and the desire for a visually curated and controlled urban environment.","The Wickquasgeck Trail is an example of a historical desire path, created by Native Americans to cross the forests of Manhattan and move between settlements quickly. This trail, when Dutch colonists arrived, was widened and made into one of the main trade roads across the island, known at the time as de Heere Straat, or Gentlemen’s Street. Following the British assumption of control in New York, the street was renamed Broadway. Notably, Broadway stands out as one of the few areas in NYC that defies the grid-based system applied to the rest of the city, cutting a diagonal across parts of the city.","In online spaces, desire paths have sparked a fascination that can approach obsession, with the Reddit page serving as a hub. Contributors offer a wide array of stories, from little-known new shortcuts to long-established alternate routes.","Animal desire paths, such as ducks forging trails through frozen ponds or dogs carving direct routes in gardens, highlight the adaptability of these trails in both human and animal experiences. As desire paths criss-cross through both physical and virtual landscapes, they stand as a proof of the collective insistence on forging unconventional routes and embracing the spirit of communal choice."],"questions":[{"q_num":36,"stem":"According to Paragraph 1, desire paths are a result of ____.","options":{"A":"the curiosity to explore surrounding hills","B":"the necessity to preserve green spaces","C":"the tendency to pursue convenience","D":"the wish to find comfort in solitude"},"answer":"C","hint":{"para":1,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第1段：欲望路径揭示人们共享的捷径（shared shortcuts），通过抄近路、穿草坪越山丘，体现人类（及动物）以最高效方式从A点到达B点的天性（go from point A to point B most effectively），即追求便利的倾向。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偷换概念】第1段提到小径“跨越山丘（cross hills）”，是为了走最近路线抄近道，并非出于“探索周边山丘的好奇心（curiosity to explore）”。","B":"【正反混淆】第1段称这些土路往往穿过原本整洁的绿地并把草坪一分为二（bisect lawns），并非出于“保护绿地的必要性（preserve green spaces）”。","C":"【正解】第1段指出欲望路径体现了人们“共享的捷径（shared shortcuts）”，并展现人类以最高效方式从A点到B点的自然能力（go from point A to point B most effectively），精准对应 the tendency to pursue convenience（追求便利的倾向）。","D":"【无中生有】第1段强调的是“集体选择（collective choices）”，完全未提及“在独处中寻找慰藉（comfort in solitude）”。"}},{"q_num":37,"stem":"It can be inferred that Ohio State University ____.","options":{"A":"intends to improve its desire paths","B":"leads in the research on desire paths","C":"guides the creation of its desire paths","D":"takes a positive view of desire paths"},"answer":"D","hint":{"para":2,"type":"推断题","focus":"定位第2段第二句：俄亥俄州立大学先允许学生自由穿行校园中央椭圆草坪，随后直接沿着学生踩出的欲望路径铺设步道，形成高效路网——由此可推知该校对欲望路径持肯定积极态度。"},"question_type":"推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偷换概念】该校是把学生自然踩出的路径直接硬化铺成正式步道（pave the desire paths），重点在于顺应与接纳而非“试图改良既有欲望路径的设计”。","B":"【无中生有】第2段仅将该校作为善用欲望路径的实践案例，并未说明该校在欲望路径研究领域处于领先地位（leads in the research）。","C":"【正反混淆】原文明确说学校“允许学生自由穿行（allowed its students to navigate... freely）”，并非事先人为引导（guides）欲望路径的产生。","D":"【正解】第2段指出俄亥俄州立大学放手让学生在草坪上自由行走，随后顺应学生踩出的高效路线直接铺设道路（proceeded to pave the desire paths），与第3段持抵触态度的规划师形成鲜明对比，可推断该校对欲望路径持积极态度（takes a positive view of desire paths）。"}},{"q_num":38,"stem":"The images on the Reddit webpage reflect ____.","options":{"A":"conflicting opinions on the use of desire paths","B":"the call to upgrade the designing of public spaces","C":"the demand for proper planning of desire paths","D":"growing concerns over the loss of public spaces"},"answer":"A","hint":{"para":3,"type":"细节推断题","focus":"定位第3段后两句：Reddit网页展示了各地欲望路径旁竖着要求行人走指定步道的指示牌，凸显其叛逆特质，紧接着指出“这一冲突凸显了公共空间自发演进与追求受控美观城市环境之间的持续博弈（This clash highlights an ongoing struggle...）”。"},"question_type":"细节推断题","option_analysis":{"A":"【正解】第3段指出，Reddit网页上展示的图片里既有行人踩出的欲望路径，又有要求行人走指定步道的告示牌，紧接着明确点明：“This clash highlights an ongoing struggle between the organic, user-driven evolution of public spaces and the desire for a visually curated and controlled urban environment.”这正是对欲望路径使用看法的直接冲突（conflicting opinions on the use of desire paths）。","B":"【无中生有】图片展现的是使用者与管理者之间的拉锯冲突，并未体现“呼吁升级公共空间设计（call to upgrade）”。","C":"【偷换概念】第3段明确将指示牌与野路并存称为“rebellious nature”和“clash / ongoing struggle”，并非表达对“妥善规划欲望路径的需求（demand for proper planning）”。","D":"【无中生有】第3段提到规划师担心安全、环境和美观，并未提及公众担忧“公共空间的丧失（loss of public spaces）”。"}},{"q_num":39,"stem":"The example of the Wickquasgeck Trail illustrates ____.","options":{"A":"the growth of New York City","B":"the Dutch origin of desire paths","C":"the importance of urban planning","D":"the recognition of desire paths"},"answer":"D","hint":{"para":4,"type":"例证题","focus":"定位第4段：原住民在曼哈顿森林中走出的快捷小径Wickquasgeck Trail，先被荷兰殖民者拓宽为主贸易干道，后被英国人更名为百老汇（Broadway），并打破纽约网格格局保留至今，生动印证了欲望路径被正式接纳认可的历史。"},"question_type":"例证题","option_analysis":{"A":"【偏离主题】纽约城的历史变迁只是该典故的时间背景，举此例并非为了说明纽约的城市扩张（growth of New York City）。","B":"【张冠李戴】第4段首句明言该小径由美洲原住民（Native Americans）开辟，荷兰殖民者只是后来将其拓宽，说“荷兰起源（Dutch origin）”张冠李戴。","C":"【正反混淆】第4段末句特别指出百老汇恰恰“违背了纽约其余地区的网格规划系统（defies the grid-based system）”，并非用来论证城市规划的重要性。","D":"【正解】第4段讲述原住民踩出的历史欲望路径Wickquasgeck Trail先后被荷兰人拓宽为主干道、被英国人命名为著名的百老汇并打破网格规划保留下来，充分展现了欲望路径获得正式承认与接纳的过程（the recognition of desire paths）。"}},{"q_num":40,"stem":"It can be learned from the last paragraph that desire paths ____.","options":{"A":"reveal humans’ deep respect for nature","B":"are crucial to humans’ mental well-being","C":"are a human imitation of animal behaviour","D":"show a shared trait in humans and animals"},"answer":"D","hint":{"para":6,"type":"细节题","focus":"定位第6段首句：鸭子在冰面踏出小道、狗在花园走出捷径等动物欲望路径，凸显了这类小径在人类和动物经验中的共同适应性（in both human and animal experiences），即展现了人与动物共有的特质。"},"question_type":"细节题","option_analysis":{"A":"【无中生有】末段并列探讨人与动物踩出小径的行为，并未提及人类“对自然的深切敬畏（deep respect for nature）”。","B":"【无中生有】末段完全未提及欲望路径对人类心理健康（mental well-being）至关重要。","C":"【偷换概念】末段说欲望路径在人类和动物经验中都具适应性，并非说人类是在“模仿动物行为（human imitation of animal behaviour）”。","D":"【正解】第6段首句以鸭子和狗踏出捷径为例，指出“Animal desire paths... highlight the adaptability of these trails in both human and animal experiences”，与第1段“people (and animals)”遥相呼应，说明欲望路径体现了人类与动物共有的特征（show a shared trait in humans and animals）。"}}],"detailed_analysis":"本文以城市规划中的“欲望路径（Desire Paths）”为主题。首段界定其为人们为抄近道、以最高效方式从A点到B点而踩出的非官方小径；第2–3段对比了俄亥俄州立大学顺势铺路的积极态度与另一些规划师因审美和安全顾虑设立禁行牌的抵制，折射出民众自发演进与官方可控规划的冲突；第4段以曼哈顿原住民小径Wickquasgeck Trail最终演变为百老汇大道为例，展示欲望路径获得正式认可的历史；末两段延伸至网络热潮与动物踩出的小径，凸显人与动物在开辟捷径上的共同特质。","keywords":[{"word":"desire path","trans":"n. 欲望路径，自发小道"},{"word":"pavement","trans":"n. 人行道，铺面"},{"word":"organic","trans":"adj. 有机的，自然的"},{"word":"top-down","trans":"adj. 自上而下的"},{"word":"geometry","trans":"n. 几何学，几何形态"},{"word":"spontaneity","trans":"n. 自发性，随性"}]}];
